hadiths[600]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1","Book of Purification, Chapter of Waters (1). Abu Ya'la said: al-Himmani narrated to us, Sharik narrated, from al-Miqdam ibn Shurayh, from his father, from A'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her) who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Water, nothing makes it impure. Al-Bazzar said: we do not know it raised (to the Prophet) except from Sharik. I (Ibn Hajar) say: its chain is good (hasan), for al-Himmani, that is Yahya, is not alone in it."
"2","Musaddad said: Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Shu'bah, from Qatadah, from Kurayb, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) regarding ablution from sea water, who said: They are the two seas; it does not harm you with whichever of them you begin. This is halted (mawquf); its men are trustworthy."
"3","Chapter of the amount of water sufficient for ablution and bathing (3). Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah said: Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Husayn, from Yazid al-Raqashi, from a woman of his people, that when she performed Hajj she would pass by Umm Salamah (may Allah be pleased with her). She said: I said to her: Show me the vessel in which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would perform ablution. She brought it out, and I said: this is the makkuk of the mufti. Then I said: show me the vessel in which he would bathe. She brought it out, and I said: this is the qafiz of the mufti; it is the cup of the travellers. In its chain there is criticism: Yazid is weak, and the woman's condition I do not know."
"4","Al-Harith said: Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr narrated to us, Za'idah narrated, from Husayn ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Yazid al-Raqashi, from a woman of his people who said: I entered upon Umm Salamah (may Allah be pleased with her) and said: show me, and she mentioned it; in it she said about the bathing vessel: this is sealed, meaning the sa', and about the ablution vessel she said: this is a quarter of the mufti('s measure). In its chain there is softness."
"5","Abu Bakr said: al-Fadl ibn Dukayn narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Hafs al-Attar narrated, from al-Bahiyy, from al-Suddi, from A'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her) who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution from a kouz (mug). Its chain is good (hasan)."
"6","Abu Ya'la said: Surayj ibn Yunus narrated to us, Ali ibn Thabit narrated, from al-Salt ibn Dinar, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Abu Umamah (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): he performed ablution with half a mudd. In its chain there is criticism."
"7","Chapter of the pond in which carrion falls, and the ruling of stagnant water (7). Musaddad said: Isma'il narrated to us, Awf narrated, a shaykh who used to judge among us in the mosque of the shaykhs before the battle of Ibn al-Ash'ath narrated to me, who said: it reached me that the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) were on a journey and came to a pond with carrion in one side of it, so they held back from it until the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to them. They said: O Messenger of Allah, this pond has carrion in one side of it. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Give drink and take water, for water is made lawful and is not made unlawful. Its chain is weak."
"8","Ibn Abi Shaybah said: Ali ibn Hashim narrated to us."
"9","Ahmad ibn Mani' said: Hushaym narrated to us, both of them from Ibn Abi Layla, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: We used to like to take water from the pond and bathe with it at a side, because of the prohibition of urinating into stagnant water."
"10","Ishaq said: Sufyan informed us, from Manbudh, from his mother who said: We used to travel with Maymunah, and she would stop at ponds containing dung-beetles and droppings, and we would draw water for her from them, and she saw no harm in that."
"11","Chapter of used water (10). Musaddad: Mu'tamir narrated to us, I heard my father say: I heard a shaykh narrating from Jabir ibn Amr (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought water, and the water was little, so he performed ablution inside the vessel, then ordered that it be sprinkled over the people, and whoever was touched by that water rejoiced in himself. He said: and I deem it touched all the people. Then he stood and prayed the dawn prayer with them. In its chain is an (unnamed) shaykh."
"12","Abu Ya'la said: Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Abi Uways narrated, Kharijah ibn al-Harith narrated to me, from Salim ibn Sarj, from the daughter of Qays, that is Khawlah, the grandmother of Kharijah ibn al-Harith, that he heard her say: My hand and the hand of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would differ (alternate) in one vessel. The hadith of Hudhayfah (may Allah be pleased with him) comes in the chapter of covering oneself while bathing, God willing; its men are trustworthy."
"13","Chapter of removing impurities (12/1). Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah said: I was told from Ibn Idris, from Layth, that is Ibn Abi Sulaym, from Hudayr, freedman of Banu Abs, from the freedman of Zaynab bint Jahsh (may Allah be pleased with them both) called Abu al-Qasim, from Zaynab bint Jahsh (may Allah be pleased with her) who said: While the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was in my house, Husayn (may Allah be pleased with him) came as a boy and sat on the belly of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then placed his penis in his navel. I stood toward him, and he said: Bring me water. I brought him water and he poured it over it, then said: The urine of the girl is washed, and water is poured over (the urine of) the boy. It is sahih; Abu Dawud, al-Nasa'i and al-Hakim reported it from the hadith of Abu al-Samh, its end with other than this wording, the meaning being one."
"14","Abu Ya'la said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Salih al-Azdi narrated to us, Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulayman narrated, from Layth ibn Abi Sulaym, from Hudayr ibn al-Hasan al-Absi, from a freedman of Zaynab or from some of her family, from Zaynab (may Allah be pleased with them both) who said: While the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was in my house, and Husayn (may Allah be pleased with him) was with me when he had begun to walk, I was heedless of him and he entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and sat on his belly and urinated. I went to take him, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) woke and said: Leave him. So I left him until he finished. Then he called for water and said: From the boy it is poured, and from the girl it is washed, so pour a pouring. Then he performed ablution and stood to pray; when he stood he embraced him to himself, and when he bowed or sat he put him down, then he sat supplicating and wept, then stretched his hand. I said when he finished the prayer: O Messenger of Allah, I saw you today do something I never saw you do. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Gabriel (peace be upon him) came to me and told me that this son of mine will be killed by my ummah. I said: Show me his soil, and he showed me his soil, red."
"15","Ahmad ibn Mani' said: Ibn Ulayyah narrated to us, Umarah ibn Abi Hafsah narrated, from Abu Mijlaz, from Hasan ibn Ali, or that Husayn ibn Ali (was involved): a woman of my family narrated to us, who said: While the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was lying on his back playing with a boy on his chest, he urinated. She stood to take him and strike him, and he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Leave him; bring me a mug of water. He sprinkled water over the urine until the water flowed over the urine, and said (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): This is what is done with urine: it is sprinkled from the male and washed from the female."
"16","Abu Ya'la said: Abu al-Rabi' narrated to us, Isma'il, meaning Ibn Ulayyah, narrated, Isma'il narrated, from al-Hasan, from his mother, from Umm Salamah (may Allah be pleased with her) who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Water is poured over the urine of the boy, and the urine of the girl is washed."
"17","Hawtharah narrated to us, Mubarak narrated, from al-Hasan, from his mother, from Umm Salamah (may Allah be pleased with her) with it. He added: as long as he has not eaten; and he added: whether she has eaten or not; and he did not raise it (to the Prophet)."
"18","Abu Hisham al-Rifa'i narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated, Sam'an ibn Malik narrated, from Abu Wa'il, from Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: A Bedouin came and urinated in the mosque, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered his spot to be dug up, and a bucket of water was poured over it. Al-Bukhari and Muslim reported it with the meaning of this hadith from Anas ibn Malik; sahih."
"19","Ishaq said: al-Nadr ibn Shumayl informed us, Abu al-Awwam al-Bahili Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Rabi' narrated, Abu al-Zubayr informed us, from Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey, and he came upon two graves whose occupants were being punished. He said: They are not being punished for something major. Then he said: Rather: as for one of them, he used to backbite people, and as for the other, he would not shield himself from his urine. Then he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took a moist palm stalk, or two stalks, and broke them, then planted each piece upon a grave, and said: It will be lightened for them as long as they remain moist, or he said: as long as they do not dry. Al-Bukhari and Muslim reported it with other than this context; sahih."
"20","Ishaq said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad al-Darawardi informed us, Safwan ibn Sulaym informed me, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about dry dung which a man treads upon, and he said: That clean ground purifies him. This is mursal or mu'dal."
"21","Chapter of the leftover of the cat and other pure animals (18). Musaddad: Yahya narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Harmalah, my mother narrated to me, who said: I was with Umm Salamah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, may Allah be pleased with her), when a dish of bread and meat was gifted to her. She stood for prayer and we stood to pray, then a cat came to the food and ate from it. When we finished, Umm Salamah (may Allah be pleased with her) took the bowl and rounded it (broke off) until (removing) where the cat had eaten from its side, then ate from it."
"22","He also said: Abdullah ibn Dawud narrated to us, from Sufyan and Hasan ibn Salih, from al-Rukayn ibn al-Rabi', from his paternal aunt, who said: al-Hasan ibn Ali (may Allah be pleased with them both) said: There is no harm in the leftover of the cat."
"23","Abdullah narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Muslim, from his father, from Abu Sa'id al-Jabiri, who said: Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) was asked: the cat drinks from the vessel? He said: There is no harm in the leftover of the cat. It is reported raised (to the Prophet) with the authors of the four Sunan and Ibn Khuzaymah in his Sahih, from Abu Qatadah (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said regarding the cat: It is not impure; it is of those that go around you, male and female. Sahih."
"24","Chapter of the purity of musk (21). Abu Ya'la said: Abu Hammam al-Walid ibn Shuja' narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Umar al-Ansari of Banu Bayadah narrated to me, Ayyub ibn Abdullah narrated to me, from Ibrahim ibn Isma'il ibn Mujammi', from a freedman of Salamah ibn al-Akwa', from Salamah (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would take musk and wipe his head and beard with it."
"25","Chapter of the purity of phlegm and tears (22). Abu Ya'la: Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr narrated to us, Thabit ibn Hammad Abu Zayd narrated, Ali ibn Zayd narrated, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Ammar (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by me while I was watering a she-camel of mine before me. I spat, and my phlegm hit my garment, so I started washing my garment from the small water-skin before me. He said: O Ammar, your phlegm and your eye tears are but like the water in your skin; only urine and stool are washed off, and semen from the greater water (i.e. ghusl), and blood and vomit."
"26","Chapter of vessels (23). Abu Ya'la said: Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Husayn ibn Ali narrated, from Muhammad ibn Ali his brother, from Muhammad ibn Isma'il who said: I entered upon Anas ibn Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) and saw with him a wooden cup. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to drink from it and perform ablution (from it)."
"27","Abu Ya'la said: Hafs ibn Abdullah Abu Umar al-Hulwani narrated to us, Darust ibn Ziyad narrated, from Yazid al-Raqashi, from Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: I was walking with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he said: O my son, call for ablution water for me from this house. I said: The Messenger of Allah is asking for ablution water. He said: Tell him that his bucket is the skin of a dead animal. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Ask them: did they tan it? They said: Yes. He said: Its tanning is its purification."
"28","Muhammad ibn Bakkar narrated to us, Faraj ibn Fadalah narrated, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Amrah, from Umm Salamah (may Allah be pleased with her) who said: A sheep of ours which we used to milk died, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked us about it, saying: What happened to your sheep, O Umm Salamah? She said: I said: It died, and we threw it away. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Why did you not benefit from its hide? She said: It was said: O Messenger of Allah, it is carrion. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Its tanning made it lawful just as vinegar made wine lawful. Faraj said: meaning that when wine changes and becomes vinegar, it becomes lawful."
"29","Al-Harith said: Asim ibn Ali narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Rashid al-Khuza'i narrated, from Sulayman ibn Musa, from Ata, from Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: With the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) we would obtain from our spoils from the polytheists water-skins and vessels, and we would distribute them all as carrion (i.e. regarding their ruling)."
"30","Musaddad said: Abdullah ibn Dawud narrated to us, Habib ibn Jurayy narrated, from Abu Ja'far who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to like the enclosed (lidded fitting) vessel."
"31","Yahya narrated to us, from Sufyan, Habib ibn Abi Thabit narrated to me, from a man, from Umm Muslim al-Ashja'iyyah (may Allah be pleased with her) who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon me while I was in a dome (tent), and said: What a fine dome, if only there were no carrion in it."
"32","Musaddad said: Yahya narrated to us, from Sadaqah ibn al-Muthanna, my grandfather Riyah ibn al-Harith narrated to me, who said: Ibn Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) was in the mosque with people reciting to him, and he called for a drink, saying: This drink was in the skin of a milch ewe of ours that died."
"33","Abu Ya'la said: Muhammad ibn Bahr narrated to us, Sulaym ibn Muslim narrated, al-Nadr ibn Arabi narrated, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever drinks in vessels of gold and silver only gurgles in his belly the fire of Hell. Al-Bukhari and Muslim reported it in their Sahihs from Umm Salamah. The hadith of Abu Uthman about the vessels of the polytheists comes in his biography in the Book of Merits, God willing."
"34","Chapter on the command to cover vessels at night (31). Abu Ya'la said: Ibrahim, that is Ibn al-Hajjaj, narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muslim narrated, from al-A'mash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: A man called Abu Humayd brought the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a vessel containing milk from al-Naqi' by day, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Why did you not cover it, even by laying a stick across it. Sahih; what is preserved is from the hadith of Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him)."
"35","Al-Harith said: Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, Ibn Abi Layla narrated, from Ikrimah ibn Khalid, from a man of the family of Abu Wada'ah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked for drink while circumambulating the House, and one of them said: Shall I bring you a drink we make? He said: Yes. He was brought a vessel containing nabidh, and he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Why did you not turn a vessel over it and lay a stick across it. He said: He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) drank from it and frowned, then called for water and poured it over it, then drank and gave him to drink."
"36","Chapter of cleaning oneself (33). Abu Ya'la said: Abu Bakr al-Ramadi narrated to us, Ibn Abi Maryam narrated, Nafi', meaning Ibn Umar, that is al-Jumahi, narrated, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would go to relieve himself to al-Mughammas. Nafi' said: about two miles from Mecca."
"37","Muhammad ibn Bakkar narrated to us, Yusuf ibn Atiyyah narrated, from Ata ibn Abi Maymunah, from Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he went out for his need would go far away so that no one would see him."
"38","Al-Harith ibn Abi Usamah said: Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Zayd narrated, from Wasil, freedman of Abu Uyaynah, from Yahya ibn Ubayd, from his father, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would choose a place for his urine as he would choose for his dwelling."
"39","Sa'id ibn Ya'qub al-Isbahani said in his book on the Companions: Sahl ibn al-Farrukhan narrated to us, Ibn Abi al-Sarri narrated, Waki' narrated, from Sa'id ibn Zayd, from Wasil, freedman of Abu Uyaynah, from Ubayd ibn Sayfi, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He mentioned the hadith, so from this it was necessary to give Sayfi a biography among the Companions."
"40","Al-Hakam ibn Musa narrated to us, al-Walid, that is Ibn Muslim, narrated, from al-Walid ibn Sulayman ibn Abi al-Sa'ib, from Talhah ibn Abi Qanan, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he wanted to urinate and came to rugged ground would take a stick and poke the earth with it until he stirred up dust, then urinate in it."
"41","Ahmad ibn Mani' said: Yazid, that is Ibn Harun, narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Fadl ibn Atiyyah narrated, from Zayd al-Ammi, from Ja'far al-Abdi, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The screen between the eyes of the jinn and the private parts of the sons of Adam, when a man removes his garment, is to say: In the name of Allah. Muhammad is weak; Sa'id ibn Maslamah opposed him, from al-A'mash, from Zayd al-Ammi, from Anas (may Allah be pleased with him). Ibn Adi and al-Tabarani reported it in al-Da'awat and al-Awsat."
"42","Abu Ya'la said: al-Qawariri narrated to us, Yusuf ibn Khalid narrated, Amr ibn Sufyan ibn Abi al-Bakarat narrated to me, from Mahfuz ibn Alqamah, from al-Hadrami, who was among the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that a Bedouin met the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asking him about relieving oneself, and he said: Do not face the qiblah nor turn your back to it when you clean yourself. He said: O Messenger of Allah, what shall I do? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Turn sideways with two stones and join the third. Yusuf is abandoned (matruk)."
"43","With this chain: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade a man to clean himself with his right hand. Ibn Qani' reported it in the biography of Hadrami ibn Amir al-Asadi, limited to the second, adding: and do not face the wind."
"44","Musaddad: Yahya narrated to us, Zakariyya narrated, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Rufay', from Mujahid, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never urinated standing except once, in a sand heap he liked."
"45","Abu Ya'la said: Bundar narrated to us, Abd al-Kabir ibn Abd al-Majid narrated, Abdullah ibn Nafi' narrated, from his father, from Usamah ibn Zayd (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade facing the qiblah with stool or urine."
"46","Al-Rifa'i narrated to us, Abu Bakr al-Hanafi narrated, with it, and in it that Usamah (may Allah be pleased with him) informed him, with the wording: Do not face (the qiblah). Ayyub opposed him, narrating it from Nafi', from a man of the Ansar, from his father (may Allah be pleased with him). Ahmad, Ibn Abi Shaybah and Musaddad reported it."
"47","Musaddad said: Yahya narrated to us, from Imran ibn Hudayr, from a man among the maternal uncles of al-Muharrar ibn Abi Hurayrah, that he saw Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) urinate standing while wearing two dyed garments, then call for water and wash what was there."
"48","Yahya narrated to me, Wiqa' ibn Iyas narrated, Abu Zibyan narrated to me, who said: I saw Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) urinate standing in al-Rahbah, then perform ablution and wipe over his sandals, and enter the mosque."
"49","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah said: Malik ibn Isma'il narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated, Wahb ibn Uqbah narrated, from Muhammad ibn Sa'd al-Ansari, from his father, from Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) that he came to al-Mihras and urinated standing, then performed ablution and wiped over his leather socks, then headed to the mosque. I said to him: You have done something disliked? He said: I served the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) nine years doing that."
"50","He also said: Qutaybah ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Ya'qub ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated, from Abu Hazim, that he saw Sahl ibn Sa'd (may Allah be pleased with him) urinate the urine of a very old man while standing, almost preceding him, then perform ablution and wipe over the two leather socks. I said: Will you not remove the leather socks? He said: No; I saw one better than me and you wipe over them, meaning the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Its chain is sahih."
"51","Al-Harith said: Abu Asim narrated to us, Ibn Awn narrated, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, who said: While Sa'd ibn Ubadah (may Allah be pleased with him) was standing urinating, he died; the jinn killed him. And they said:"
"52","Musaddad said: Yahya narrated to us, from Qurrah ibn Khalid, from Budayl, from Mutarrif, a Bedouin narrated to me, who said: I accompanied Abu Dharr (may Allah be pleased with him), and all his manners pleased me, except that when he entered the toilet he would sprinkle (water)."
"53","Abu Bakr said: Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Asadi narrated to us, from Zam'ah ibn Salih, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to me, from a man of Banu Mudlij, from his father, who said: Suraqah ibn Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) came and began saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) taught us such and such. One of the people said to him: How did he teach you to defecate? He said: Yes; he commanded us to lean upon the right and erect the left."
"54","Ahmad ibn Mani' said: Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri narrated to us with this, but he reversed it regarding the right and the left."
"55","Abd ibn Humayd said: Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, from Isra'il, from Abu Yahya, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Most of the punishment of the grave is from urine, so keep yourselves clean from urine."
"56","Musaddad said: Yahya narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Three stones suffice for cleaning oneself."
"57","Ibn Abi Umar said: al-Muqri narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Ziyad ibn An'um narrated, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Rafi', from Abdullah, that is Ibn Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: I was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the night of the jinn, and I heard them asking him for a ruling about cleaning oneself, and I heard him say: Three stones. They said: What about water? He said: It is purer and purer."
"58","Ahmad ibn Mani' said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ziyad ibn An'um, with it."
"59","Abu Ya'la said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyibi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Nafi' narrated to me, from Abdullah ibn Nafi', freedman of Ibn Umar, from his father, from Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) that delegations of the jinn from the island came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and stayed with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Then it occurred to them to return to their land, so they asked him to provision them. He said: I have nothing with which to provision you, but draw near to every bone you pass by, it is broad meat for you, and every dung you pass by, it is fruit for you. Therefore he forbade wiping oneself with dung and decayed bone."
"60","Abu Ya'la said: Ahmad ibn Imran al-Akhnasi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated, Ibrahim al-Hajari narrated, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Allah is Odd and loves the odd, so when you clean yourself with stones, make it odd."
"61","He said: Mu'alla ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Uthman ibn Matar narrated, from Ali ibn al-Hakam, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Upon you is thorough cleaning of the anus, for it removes piles."
"62","Chapter of the description of ablution (54/1). Ibn Abi Umar said: Bishr, that is Ibn al-Sari, narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Sumay', from Abu Umamah (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would wash his hands three times, rinse his mouth three times, sniff water three times three times, wash his face three times, and his forearms three times three times."
"63","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah said: Yazid ibn Harun narrated, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated, and he mentioned it with the wording: He performed ablution and washed his hands three times, rinsed his mouth three times, and sniffed water three times."
"64","Ahmad ibn Mani' said: Yazid narrated to us, the same, adding: And he performed ablution three times three times."
"65","Abu Ya'la said: Kamil ibn Talhah narrated to us, Hammad narrated, the same as the hadith of Bishr."
"66","Ahmad ibn Mani' said: al-Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Abu al-Nadr narrated, from one who saw Uthman ibn Affan, who said: Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him) called for ablution water, with Ali and Talhah (may Allah be pleased with them both) present, and performed ablution three times three times. Then he said: I adjure you by Allah, do you know that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to perform ablution as I performed? They said: Yes."
"67","Al-Harith said: Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Layth, that is Ibn Sa'd, narrated, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Abu al-Nadr, who said: Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him) called for ablution water, with Talhah, al-Zubayr, Sa'd and Ali (may Allah be pleased with them) present. Then he performed ablution while they looked on, mentioning in it ablution three times three times. Then he said to those present: I adjure you by Allah, do you know that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to perform ablution as I have just performed? They said: Yes. And that was because of something that reached him about the ablution of (certain) men."
"68","Abu Ya'la said: Ghassan ibn al-Rabi' narrated to us, al-Layth ibn Sa'd narrated, with it."
"69","Abd ibn Humayd said: Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, al-Mukhtar ibn Nafi' narrated, from Abu Matar, who said: While we were sitting with Ali (may Allah be pleased with him), a man said to him: Show me the ablution of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He called Qanbar and said: Bring me a mug of water. He washed his hands and face three times, put some of his fingers into his mouth, and mentioned the hadith; in it: the outside of the ears is of the head and their inside is of the face. Then he sipped a sip after ablution, then said: Such was the ablution of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"70","Musaddad said: Muhammad ibn Jabir narrated to us, from Damdam, from his father (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution and wiped his head once."
"71","Abu Bakr said: Hafs narrated to us, from Layth, from Talhah, from his father, from his grandfather, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) perform ablution and wipe his head like this, and Hafs passed his hand over his head until he wiped his nape."
"72","Abd ibn Humayd said: Zakariyya ibn Adi narrated to me, Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated, and he mentioned it with the wording: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) perform ablution; he placed his hand above his head, then returned it to his nape, then brought it out from under the chin."
"73","Chapter of the obligation of ablution (59). Al-Harith said: Dawud ibn al-Muhabbar narrated to us, Hammad narrated, from Ayyub and Humayd, or one of them, from Abu Qilabah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah does not accept prayer without purification, nor charity from misappropriation."
"74","And from Hammad, from Humayd and others, from al-Hasan (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the same."
"75","Chapter of the tooth-stick (61). Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah said: Abu Khalid al-Ahmar narrated to us, from Wasil, Abu Sawrah ibn Abi Ayyub narrated to me, from Abu Ayyub (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to use the tooth-stick repeatedly at night."
"76","Ibn Abi Umar said: Waki' narrated to us, al-Mundhir ibn Tha'labah al-Abdi narrated, from Ibn Buraydah, from his father (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he woke at night would call a slave-girl called Barirah, for the tooth-stick."
"77","Ibn Abi Shaybah said: Abu Khalid al-Ahmar narrated to us, from Haram ibn Uthman, from Abu Atiq, from Jabir, that he would use the tooth-stick when he lay down, when he rose at night, and when he went out to prayer. He said: I said to him: You have burdened yourself with this tooth-stick. He said: Usamah (may Allah be pleased with him) told me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to use this tooth-stick."
"78","Ahmad ibn Mani' said: al-Haytham ibn Kharijah narrated to us, Hafs ibn Maysarah narrated, from Haram ibn Uthman, with it, adding: He said: And I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Were it not that I would burden my ummah, I would have made the tooth-stick obligatory."
"79","Musaddad said: Muhammad ibn Jabir narrated to us, from Sinan ibn Habib, from a shaykh of the Hijaz, from Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr (may Allah be pleased with them both) who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Were it not that I would burden my ummah, I would command them to use the tooth-stick at every prayer."
"80","Ibn Abi Shaybah said: Muhammad ibn Hayyan narrated to us, Sulayman narrated, from Abu Habib, with it."
"81","Mu'awiyah ibn Hisham narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Qarm narrated, from Abu Habib, from a man of the Hijaz, with this."
"82","Ahmad ibn Mani' said: Yusuf ibn Atiyyah narrated to us, from al-Ala ibn Kathir, from Makhul, from Wathilah ibn al-Asqa' (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: The Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would fasten their tooth-sticks in the tassels of their swords, and the women in their headscarves."
"83","Abu Ya'la said: Ubaydullah narrated to us, Yusuf ibn Khalid narrated, from al-A'mash, from Anas ibn Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would use the tooth-stick with the leftover of his ablution (water)."
"84","Al-Bazzar said: Khalid ibn Yusuf narrated to us, my father narrated, with it. Yusuf is al-Samti, very weak."
"85","Abu Ya'la said: Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated, Hammad narrated, from Ibn Abi Atiq, from his father, from Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The tooth-stick is a purification for the mouth, pleasing to the Lord."
"86","Abd al-A'la ibn Hammad narrated to us, saying Hammad ibn Salamah narrated, with this. Abd al-A'la said: It is a mistake; what is correct is: from Ibn Abi Atiq, from A'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her)."
"87","Al-Harith: al-Hakam ibn Musa narrated to us, Isa ibn Yunus narrated, Abu Bakr ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Maryam narrated, from Damrah ibn Habib (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade using the tooth-stick of sweet basil wood, saying: It stirs the vein of leprosy."
"88","Chapter of the qualities of fitrah (69). Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi said: Quraysh ibn Hayyan narrated to us, from Wasil, who said: I came to Abu Ayyub al-Azdi and shook his hand, and he saw my nails long. He said: A man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asking him, and he said: One of you asks me about the news of heaven while leaving his nails like the claws of birds, in which janabah and dirt gather. Al-Bayhaqi said: This Abu Ayyub is a follower (tabi'i), and the hadith is mursal. Yunus ibn Habib, the narrator from Abu Dawud, said: Abu Mas'ud, meaning al-Razi, reported it from al-Aqadi, from Quraysh, from Sulayman ibn Farrukh, who said: I met Abu Ayyub, and mentioned it, without saying al-Azdi."
"89","Musaddad said: Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, Hafs ibn Abi Dawud narrated, Asim ibn Bahdalah narrated to me, who said: I saw Shaqiq trim his hair, then enter the mosque and pray Zuhr and Asr without touching water."
"90","Hushaym narrated to us, from Yunus, from Ibrahim, who said: We wipe it with water."
"91","Abdullah ibn Dawud narrated to us, from Fitr, from Bashir, (who said) Ibrahim said: Whatever iron touches of nail or hair, touch it with water."
"92","Ibn Dawud narrated to us, from a shaykh called Abu Abdullah, from Umar ibn Qays, who said: Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) said: It only increases him in purity, meaning trimming hair and nails."
"93","Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Husayn, from Ali al-Azdi, who said: I heard Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) say to the barber: Boy, reach the two bones. When he shaved him, he gave him his forearms and chest, and he shaved hair upon them while people looked on. Salim said to him: Father, people think it is sunnah? He said: Tell people it is not sunnah, but Ibn Umar was bothered by his hair and wanted to lighten it from himself."
"94","Abu Ya'la said: Zuhayr narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Yazid narrated, from Musa ibn Ulayy, from his father, who said: Ibrahim (peace be upon him) was commanded and circumcised himself with a qadum (adze/place), and it was hard upon him. Allah revealed to him: You hastened before We commanded you its tool. He said: My Lord, I disliked delaying Your command."
"95","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated, from Jarir ibn Hazim, from Ibn Sirin, who said: The carpenter (najjar) was only called najjar because he was circumcised with the qadum."
"96","Abu Ya'la said: Abu Sa'id al-Ashajj narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Sulayman narrated, from Mu'awiyah ibn Yahya, from Yunus ibn Maysarah, from Abu Idris, from Abu al-Darda (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The purifiers are four: trimming the moustache, shaving the pubic hair, clipping the nails, and the tooth-stick."
"97","Chapter of remembrance over ablution (77). Al-Harith said: Abd al-Rahim ibn Waqid narrated to us, Hammad ibn Amr narrated, from al-Sari ibn Khalid ibn Shaddad, from Ja'far ibn Muhammad, from his father, from his grandfather, from Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: O Ali, when you perform ablution, say: In the name of Allah; O Allah, I ask You for completeness of ablution, completeness of prayer, completeness of Your pleasure, and completeness of Your forgiveness; this is the zakat of ablution. This hadith is very weak."
"98","Chapter of naming (Allah) (78). Abu Ya'la said: Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Ibn Abi Za'idah narrated, from Harithah ibn Muhammad, from Amrah, from A'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her) who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would rise for ablution, tip the vessel, name Allah, and perform ablution thoroughly. Harithah is weak."
"99","Chapter of the merit of thorough ablution and the merit of ablution (79/1). Ishaq said: Safwan ibn Isa informed us, al-Harith ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Dhubab informed us, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Ali ibn Abi Talib (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Thorough ablution in disliked (hard) circumstances, working the feet to the mosques, and waiting for prayer after prayer, wash away sins."
"100","Abd ibn Humayd narrated it from Safwan."
"101","Abu Ya'la narrated it from Ahmad ibn Ibrahim al-Dawraqi, from Safwan. Al-Darawardi and Abu Damrah narrated it from al-Harith, from Abu al-Ayyas, with ya' and unpointed letter, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Ali (may Allah be pleased with him). It has a witness in the Sahih from the hadith of Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), and another in the Sunan from the hadith of Abu Sa'id (may Allah be pleased with him)."
"102","Musaddad said: Attaf ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Rafi', from Anas ibn Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: I was sitting with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the mosque of al-Khayf, when two men came to him, an Ansari and a Thaqafi. He mentioned the hadith. He said: The Thaqafi said: Inform me, O Messenger of Allah. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You came to ask me about prayer: when you wash your face, sins fall from your eyelashes; when you wash your hands, sins fall from your fingernails; when you wipe your head, sins fall from your head; when you wash your feet, sins fall from your toenails. The hadith of Thawban and Abu Umamah (may Allah be pleased with them both) about thorough ablution in disliked things is in the commentary of Surah Sad. The hadith of Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) about perfecting ablution comes, God willing, in the Duha prayer. The hadith: the first for which he is reckoned is his purification, comes, God willing, at the beginning of prayer."
"103","Yahya ibn Hashim narrated to us, Ibn Abi Layla narrated, from Atiyyah, from Abu Sa'id (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: It was said: O Messenger of Allah, by what will you know your ummah on the Day of Resurrection? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Radiant, white-marked from the trace of ablution."
"104","Abu Ya'la said: Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj narrated to us, Bashshar ibn al-Hakam narrated, from Thabit, from Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: A righteous trait may be in a man, and Allah rectifies all his deeds through it; a man's purification for his prayer, Allah expiates his sins through his purification, and his prayer remains supererogatory."
"105","Al-Bazzar said: Sahl ibn Bahr narrated, Mu'alla ibn Asad narrated, Bashshar ibn al-Hakam Abu Badr al-Dabbi narrated, Thabit narrated, with it."
"106","Abu Ya'la said: Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, Mubarak, that is Ibn Suhaym, freedman of Abd al-Aziz, narrated, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Suhayb, from Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The likeness of a man is as a river from which he bathes five times; what filth may remain upon him? He rises to ablution and washes his hands, and every sin his hands did falls; he rinses his mouth, and every sin his tongue spoke falls; then he washes his face, and every sin his eyes looked at falls; then he wipes his head, and every sin his ears heard falls; then he washes his feet, and every sin his feet walked to falls."
"107","Abu Hisham narrated to us, Yahya ibn Yaman narrated, al-A'mash narrated, from Abu Salih, from Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him), raised (to the Prophet): And you are the radiant, white-marked."
"108","Abu Ya'la said: Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Abi Yazid narrated, Abbad al-Minqari narrated, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Anas ibn Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: O my son, upon you is thorough ablution; your two guardians will love you and your life will be increased. O Anas, exaggerate in sniffing water in janabah, for you leave your bath with no sin or fault upon you. I said: How is exaggeration, O Messenger of Allah? He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Wet the roots of the hair and clean the skin. O my son, if you can remain always upon ablution, for whoever death comes to while upon ablution is given martyrdom."
"109","Ahmad ibn Mani' said: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, al-Ala Abu Muhammad al-Thaqafi narrated, Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated."
"110","Chapter of the dislike of remembering Allah without ablution (86). Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from a man, from Hanzalah ibn al-Rahib, who said: A man greeted the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he did not reply until he wiped (performed tayammum/ablution), saying: Nothing prevented me from replying to you except that I was not in ablution. Or he said: he did not reply until he wiped and replied to him."
"111","Abu Ya'la said: Ubaydullah ibn Umar al-Qawariri narrated, Muhammad ibn al-Harith narrated, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Baylamani narrated, from his father, who said: I saw Uthman ibn Affan (may Allah be pleased with him) sitting at al-Maqa'id performing ablution, when a man passed and greeted him, and he did not reply until he finished his ablution. Then he entered the mosque and stood over the man, saying: Nothing prevented me from replying to you except that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever performs ablution then does not speak until he says: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah alone without partner, and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger, he is forgiven what is between the two ablutions."
"112","Chapter of concession in that (88). Ahmad ibn Mani': Hushaym narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Amr, Abu Sallam narrated, one who saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) narrated to me, who said: He urinated, then recited verses of the Qur'an before touching water."
"113","Chapter of preventing the one in ritual impurity from touching the mushaf (89). Ishaq said: Abdullah ibn Idris informed us, Muhammad ibn Umarah narrated, from Abu Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hazm, who said: In the letter which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wrote to Amr ibn Hazm when he sent him to Najran was: None touches the Qur'an except the pure, a man does not pray while tying up his hair, and none sits with legs drawn up with nothing between his private part and the sky."
"114","Chapter of running fingers through digits and beard (90). Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah said: Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulayman narrated to me, from Wasil ibn al-Sa'ib, from Abu Sawrah, from his uncle Abu Ayyub (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: How excellent are the interlacers. They said: O Messenger of Allah, who are the interlacers? He said: Interlacing in ablution is to run through between your fingers and nails, and interlacing from food, for nothing is harder upon the angel with the servant than to find the smell of food from one of you. Abu Sawrah is weak; Ahmad reported its basis."
"115","Musaddad said: Muhammad ibn Jabir narrated to us, Musa ibn Abi A'ishah narrated, from Abdullah ibn Shaddad (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution and ran his fingers through his beard, then said: Thus my Lord, mighty and majestic, commanded me to run through."
"116","Yahya narrated to us, from Sufyan, Waqid narrated to me, from Mus'ab, who said: Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) saw people performing ablution and said: Run through, meaning between the fingers."
"117","Abu Ya'la said: Masruq narrated, Ibn Abi Za'idah narrated, from Isra'il, from Amir ibn Shaqiq, from Shaqiq, who said: Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him) performed ablution and ran through his toe fingers, then said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) do that."
"118","Chapter of rinsing the mouth from milk (94). Ahmad ibn Mani' said: Isma'il, that is Ibn Ulayyah, narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Muhammad, that is Ibn Sirin, from Anas (may Allah be pleased with him), that he would rinse his mouth from milk three times. Halted (mawquf), sahih."
"119","Chapter of preferring not to seek help in purification (95). Ahmad ibn Mani' said: Abu al-Ala, that is al-Hasan ibn Sawwar, narrated to us, from Mu'awiyah ibn Salih, that Abu Hamzah narrated to him, from A'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her) who said: I never saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entrust his charity to other than himself, such that he himself would place it in the beggar's hand; nor did I see the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entrust his ablution to other than himself, such that he himself would prepare his ablution for himself when he rose at night."
"120","Abu Ya'la said: Abu Hisham narrated to us, al-Nadr, meaning Ibn Mansur, narrated, Abu al-Janub narrated, who said: I saw Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) drawing water for his ablution, and I hastened to draw for him. He said: Stop, O Abu al-Janub, for I saw Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) drawing water for his ablution, and I hastened to draw for him, and he said: Stop, O Abu al-Hasan, for I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) drawing water for his ablution, and I hastened to draw for him, and he said: Stop, O Umar, for I dislike anyone sharing in my purification."
"121","Chapter of wiping over leather socks (97). Ishaq said: Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Jarir ibn Yazid narrated, Mundhir narrated to me, Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir narrated to me, from Jabir ibn Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with them both) who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed a man performing ablution while washing his leather socks, and said (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with his hand like this: You were only commanded to wipe. He spread his fingers between his palms over his leather socks. Ibn Majah reported it; it is not in our hearing (copy)."
"122","Al-Harith said: Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated, Qatadah narrated, I heard Musa ibn Salamah: I asked Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) about wiping over leather socks? He said: Three days and their nights for the traveller, and a day and night for the resident."
"123","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah said: Hushaym ibn Bashir narrated to us, Mansur ibn Zadham narrated, from Ibn Sirin, from Aflah, freedman of Abu Ayyub, from Abu Ayyub (may Allah be pleased with him) that he would command wiping, while he himself would wash his feet. He was asked about that: How do you command wiping? He said: Evil would it be for me if its benefit is for you and its sin upon me; I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) do it and command it, but ablution (washing) endeared itself to me. Its chain is sahih."
"124","Al-Harith said: Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Layth ibn Sa'd narrated, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Sahl ibn Abi Umamah ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf al-Ansari, who said: A man of Syria asked his father Abu Umamah about wiping over leather socks? He said: Yes, wipe over them. The Syrian said: Where is the saying of Ali (may Allah be pleased with him)? My father said to me: Son, go to Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib and tell him what you said. He said: I went to him and said: My father conveys peace to you and asks you about wiping over leather socks. He said: If you put them on while pure, wipe over them until you remove them."
"125","Al-Harith also said: Muhammad ibn Umar narrated to us, Abd al-Hamid ibn Imran ibn Abi Anas narrated, from his father, from Abdullah ibn al-Tufayl, who said: I saw Amr ibn Hazm wipe over leather socks, saying: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wipe over his leather socks. The hadith of Sahl ibn Sa'd (may Allah be pleased with him) about wiping over leather socks preceded in (the chapter of) cleaning oneself."
"126","Musaddad said: Yahya narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq, from his father, from Yarim ibn al-As'ad al-Kharifi, who said: I saw Qays ibn Sa'd ibn Ubadah (may Allah be pleased with him), who had served the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ten years. He said: Then he came to Dijlah (the river) wearing two Randaj leather socks, performed ablution and wiped over his leather socks once, saying thus with his palm, with his fingers, upon the back of his leather socks."
"127","Yahya narrated to us, from Sufyan, Abu Ishaq narrated to me, from Yarim Abu al-Ala, who said: I saw Qays ibn Sa'd ibn Ubadah (may Allah be pleased with him) urinate, then come to Dijlah, perform ablution, wipe over his leather socks once, and say: Thus, with his palm, with his fingers, upon the back of his leather socks."
"128","Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Shaqiq, from Amr ibn al-Harith, who said: I went out with Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) to Medina, and he would wipe over the leather sock thrice."
"129","He said: Isma'il and Khalid narrated to us, both saying: al-Jurayri informed us, from Abu al-Ala ibn al-Shikhkhir, from Iyad ibn Nadlah, who said: We went out with Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him) in some orchards, and I needed to relieve myself, so I went for my need. I returned and sat upon a stream-bank, then Abu Musa came upon me while I wanted to remove my leather socks, and said: Leave them, and wipe until you put them off when you sleep."
"130","Musaddad said: Abd al-Warith narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Ishaq, from Anas ibn Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: We would wipe over leather socks and be commanded to. A man said to him: Did you hear it from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Do not be angry."
"131","Ahmad ibn Mani' said: Isma'il narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi Ishaq informed us, who said: I heard Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) say: We would wipe our leather socks. A man said to him: Did you hear it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: No, but we heard it from those of our companions who are not accused, saying: Wipe over leather socks, and do such and such, except that he does not use kunyah (euphemism)."
"132","Marwan ibn Mu'awiyah narrated to us, Ziyad ibn Ubaydah or Ubaydah narrated, Ahmad ibn Mani' doubted, Anas ibn Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) informed us, who said: I was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey; he rose in the pre-dawn darkness and said: O Anas, is there water in your skin? I said: Yes. He withdrew and urinated, and I poured water over him and he performed ablution. When he wanted to wipe, I bent my back to see what he would do, and he said: It is as you see, and wiped over his leather socks."
"133","Abu Ya'la said: Sahl ibn Zanjalah narrated to us, al-Sabbah ibn Muharib narrated, from Umar ibn Abdullah, that is Ibn Ya'la ibn Murrah, from his father, from his grandfather. And from Ziyad ibn Ilaqah, from Usamah ibn Sharik (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: We would be with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey, not removing our leather socks for three days and their nights for a need we fulfilled; and we would be with him in residence a day and night, wiping over our leather socks."
"134","Chapter of the manner of wiping (108). Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah said: Abu Bakr al-Hanafi narrated to us, from Abu Amir al-Khazzaz, al-Hasan narrated, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) urinate, then come and perform ablution and wipe over his leather socks, placing his right hand upon his right sock and his left hand upon his left sock, then wiping their tops a single wipe, as if I now see the trace of the fingers of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) upon the leather socks. I (Ibn Hajar) say: The hadith of al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah (may Allah be pleased with him) about wiping is in the Six Books with other than this context; Abu Amir al-Khazzaz, named Salih ibn Rustum, is weak, and al-Hasan in my view did not hear from al-Mughirah."
"135","He said: Fudayl ibn Iyad narrated to us, from Hisham, from al-Hasan, who said: Wiping over leather socks is lines with the fingers. The hadith of Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) preceded at the beginning of the chapter."
"136","Chapter of the beginning of wiping over leather socks (110). Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi said: al-Hasan ibn Wasil narrated to us, from Mu'awiyah ibn Qurrah, from Abdullah ibn Mughaffal al-Muzani, who said: The first I saw wearing leather socks in Islam was al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah (may Allah be pleased with him); he came to us while we were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), wearing two black leather socks, and he kept looking at them in admiration. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: They will become abundant for you, meaning leather socks. They said: O Messenger of Allah, what shall we do? He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You wipe over them and pray."
"137","Chapter of leaving the time limit (111). Abu Ya'la said: Ahmad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Abu Bakr al-Hanafi narrated, from Umar ibn Ishaq ibn Yasar, who said: I read to Ata a letter with him, in which was: Maymunah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), narrated to me that she said: O Messenger of Allah, does a man remove his leather socks every hour? He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No, but he wipes them as long as he wishes."
"138","Chapter of wiping over the two muq (soft boots) (112). Abu Dawud said: Ja'far ibn al-Zubayr narrated to us, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left the two muqs on his feet in the Tabuk expedition for three (days)."
"139","Chapter of sprinkling after ablution (113). Abu Ya'la said: Muhammad ibn Bakkar narrated to us, Abu Ma'shar narrated, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asking: What is thorough ablution? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was silent until prayer came. He called for water and mentioned the description of ablution. He said: Then he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sprinkled beneath his garment, saying: This is thorough ablution."
"140","Musaddad said: Sallam ibn Abi Muti' narrated to us, from Mansur ibn al-Mu'tamir, from al-Minhal ibn Amr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) who said: When one of you performs ablution, let him take a handful of water and sprinkle his private part with it; if anything befalls him, let him say: That is from it."
"141","Chapter of drying after ablution (115). Musaddad said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Mansur, from Hilal ibn Yasaf, from Ata, from Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) that he disliked it, meaning wiping the face with the towel. Sahih, halted."
"142","Chapter of what is said after ablution (116). Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah said: Husayn ibn Ali narrated to us, from Amr ibn Abdullah ibn Wahb al-Nakha'i, Abu al-Jawza narrated, from Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No Muslim servant performs ablution well, then says three times: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah alone without partner, and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger, but eight gates of Paradise are opened for him; from whichever he wishes he enters. The hadith of Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him) preceded in the chapter of the dislike of remembering Allah without ablution."
"143","Chapter of renewing ablution when one prayed with the first (117). Abu Ya'la said: Zahmawayh narrated to us, Salih ibn Umar narrated, Abu Khaldah informed us, from Abu al-Aliyah, one who used to serve the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) narrated to me, who said: This is what I memorized for you from him: When he prayed then did not leave the mosque until his (next) prayer came, he would perform a light ablution inside the mosque."
"144","Chapter of ablution-breakers (118). Musaddad said: Yahya narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Asim, from Abu Salih, who said: A'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her) said: One of you performs ablution from food, but does not perform ablution from the foul word he says?"
"145","He also said: Yahya narrated to us, from Mujalid, from Amir, from Jarir, who said: Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) led people in prayer, and something came out of a man. Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: I adjure the owner of this wind to perform ablution and repeat his prayer. Jarir (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Do you adjure everyone who heard it to perform ablution and repeat the prayer? He said: What you said is good; may Allah reward you well. So he commanded them with that."
"146","Yahya narrated to us, from Shu'bah, from Ghaylan ibn Jami', from Maymun ibn Mihran, from one who informed him, that he saw Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, insert his finger into his nose, then it came out smeared with blood, or with blood on it, then he prayed."
"147","Yahya narrated to us, from Shu'bah, from Mukhariq, from Tariq, who said: 'Abdullah, may Allah be pleased with him, said: Touching is what is less than intercourse."
"148","Chapter on laughing aloud: al-Harith: Dawud narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha', from Hafsah bint Sirin, from Abu al-'Aliyah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was praying with his Companions behind him, when a blind man came and stepped on a mat at the edge of a well and fell into the well, so the people laughed, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded whoever laughed to repeat ablution."
"149","Al-Harith said: Abu 'Asim narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, Yazid ibn Abi Khalid informed me that Abu Sufyan informed him, from Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: Whoever laughs in prayer has no ablution due upon him."
"150","Abu Ya'la said: Ibn Numayr narrated to us, from Waki', from al-A'mash, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: He was asked about a man who laughs in prayer, and he said: He repeats the prayer but does not repeat ablution."
"151","Chapter on ablution after eating what fire has touched, and explanation of its abrogation: Musaddad said: Yahya narrated to us, from Ibn Abi 'Arubah, from Qatadah, that Anas ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, used to perform ablution after eating what fire had touched, and he used to narrate that Abu Talhah, may Allah be pleased with him, performed ablution after eating what fire had touched."
"152","Ahmad ibn Mani' said: Isma'il narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from Abu Qilabah, who said: I came to Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, but did not find him, so I sat until he came; he came angry, and I spoke to him, and he said: We were with this man, meaning al-Hajjaj, and food was brought and they ate, then they stood and prayed without performing ablution, so I said: Did you not used to do this? He said: No, we did not used to do it."
"153","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Sulayman al-Taymi informed us, from Abu Qilabah, and he mentioned it, saying in it: I saw Anas ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, troubled in spirit, so I said: I see you troubled in spirit? He said: Why should I not be troubled, when I have just come from these people who ate bread and meat and prayed without performing ablution."
"154","Musaddad said: al-Mu'tamir narrated to us, I heard my father say: Abu 'Uthman narrated to us, from a man among the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Perform ablution; ablution is due after what fire has touched, and after what comes out from between dung and blood."
"155","Yahya narrated to us, from 'Ali ibn al-Mubarak, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Mahmud ibn 'Amr, from his maternal aunt or paternal aunt, Yahya doubted, and she was the wife of Zayd ibn Thabit, who said: Zayd ibn Thabit, may Allah be pleased with him, used to perform ablution after eating what fire had touched."
"156","Ishaq said: al-'Aqadi informed us, Muhammad ibn Abi Humayd narrated to us, from Hind bint Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id al-Khudri, from her paternal aunt, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ate from a sheep's shoulder, then prayed without performing ablution. I say: I think it is mursal, and Muhammad ibn Abi Humayd is weak."
"157","Yahya narrated to us, from Shu'bah, from 'Amr ibn Murrah, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: If I ate meat and drank the milk of milch camels, then prayed without performing ablution, I would not care, though I would rinse my mouth and wash my hands from the grease of food. Authentic as a stopped report."
"158","'Isa narrated to us, al-Awza'i narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) visited his daughter Fatimah, may Allah be pleased with her, and she offered him meat and he ate; when he stood up, she took hold of his cloak and said: Will you not perform ablution? He said: For what, my daughter? She said: After what fire has touched. He said: Is not the purest of our food what fire has touched? Ahmad, al-Harith, and Abu Ya'la narrated it through another chain, from Fatimah, may Allah be pleased with her, connected."
"159","Abu Ya'la said: al-Jarrah ibn Makhlad narrated to us, Musa ibn Dawud narrated to us, Husam ibn Misakk narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Ibn 'Abbas, from Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) tore meat from a shoulder with his teeth, then prayed without performing ablution."
"160","Abu al-Rabi' al-Zahrani narrated to us, Ja'far ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from Ishaq al-Hashimi: Safiyyah, may Allah be pleased with her, narrated to us, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to me and I offered him a cold shoulder, and I kept serving it to him, and he ate it, then he stood and prayed."
"161","He said: 'Abd al-Ghaffar ibn 'Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to us, 'Ali ibn Mushir narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn 'Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: I cut a shoulder for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from the pot of al-'Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, and he ate it, then stood and prayed without performing ablution."
"162","Al-Bazzar said: Ahmad ibn Aban narrated to us, 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Suhayl, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, something similar."
"163","Chapter on rinsing the mouth after milk: Ahmad ibn Mani' said: Isma'il, that is Ibn 'Ulayyah, narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Anas, that he used to rinse his mouth after milk three times. This is authentic as a stopped report."
"164","Chapter on ablution after touching the private part: Ishaq said: Muhammad ibn Bakr al-Bursani informed us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, al-Zuhri narrated to me, from 'Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr, from 'Urwah, who said, meaning al-Zuhri, though I did not hear it from him, that he used to narrate from Busrah bint Safwan, and from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: When one of you touches his penis, let him perform ablution. Ibn Jurayj said: And Yahya ibn Abi Kathir said, from a man of the Ansar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed, then returned to his seat and performed ablution, then repeated the prayer, saying: I had touched my penis and forgotten."
"165","Mu'adh ibn Hisham informed us, my father narrated to me, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, a man in the mosque of the Messenger (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) narrated to me, from 'Urwah, from 'A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: When one of you touches his penis, let him perform ablution."
"166","He also said: I read to Abu Qurrah: al-Muthanna ibn al-Sabbah mentioned, from 'Amr ibn Shu'ayb, who said: I was with Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib when touching of the penis was discussed in his presence, and Sa'id said: Busrah bint Safwan, who is one of my maternal aunts, said: I was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with so-and-so and so-and-so and 'Abdullah ibn 'Amr present, until she mentioned six or seven, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever touches his penis, let him perform ablution. As for the first chain, it is authentic and connected; the hadith of Busrah is in the four Sunan, and Ahmad transmitted it through the hadith of Zayd ibn Khalid, but through the narration of Ibn Ishaq from al-Zuhri from 'Urwah from Zayd ibn Khalid. It has become clear in the chain we cited that al-Zuhri did not hear it from 'Urwah, as if Ibn Ishaq concealed it with the concealment of leveling, since he declared hearing it from al-Zuhri; so I transmitted it through this chain for its benefit, and the remaining chains here were not transmitted by them."
"167","Al-Harith said: Yahya ibn Hashim narrated to us, Hisham ibn 'Urwah narrated to us, from 'Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from Marwan, from Busrah bint Safwan, may Allah be pleased with her, who said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about a woman touching her private part, and he said: She performs ablution."
"168","Musaddad said: Yahya narrated to us, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Harmalah, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, who said: Whoever touches his penis, ablution is due upon him."
"169","Musaddad said: Yahya narrated to us, from Sa'id, from Qatadah, who said: I asked Sa'id, meaning Ibn al-Musayyib, about touching the penis, and he said: It is like a part of your body."
"170","He said: Yahya narrated to us, from Ibn Abi 'Arubah, from Qatadah, from Abu Hassan, from Mukhariq ibn Ahmar al-Kilabi, from Hudhayfah, may Allah be pleased with him, regarding touching the penis, and he said: I do not care whether I touch it or my nose and ear. Yahya said: Or one of them."
"171","Yahya narrated to us, from Sufyan, Iyad ibn Laqit narrated to me, from al-Bara' ibn Qays, who said: Hudhayfah, may Allah be pleased with him, was asked about touching the penis, and he mentioned something similar."
"172","Abu Ya'la said: al-Jarrah ibn Makhlad narrated to us, 'Umar ibn Yunus narrated to us, al-Mufaddal ibn Thawab, a man of Yemen, narrated to us, Husayn ibn Wadda' narrated to me, from his father, from Sayf ibn 'Ubaydullah al-Himyari, who said: I and some men with me visited 'A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, and we asked her about a man touching his private part and a woman touching her private part, and she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: I do not care whether I touch it or my nose."
"173","Chapter on ablution after sleep: Ishaq: Yahya ibn Adam informed us, al-Mas'udi narrated to us, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, from 'Abdullah, who said: When one of you sleeps lying down, let him perform ablution. He was asked: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to sleep lying down and not perform ablution? He said: You are not like the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); had anything occurred from the Messenger, he would have known it."
"174","Al-Harith said: Muhammad ibn 'Umar narrated to us, Usamah ibn Zayd narrated to us, from his father Zayd ibn Aslam, from 'Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: When he lays his side down, he performs ablution."
"175","Muhammad ibn 'Umar narrated to us, Ibn Abi Sabrah narrated to us, from 'Asim ibn 'Ubaydullah, from Harmalah, freedman of Zayd, who said: I asked Zayd ibn Thabit for a ruling about sleeping while sitting, and he saw no harm in it. I said: What if I lay my side down? He said: Perform ablution."
"176","Muhammad ibn 'Umar narrated to us, Makhramah ibn Bukayr narrated to us, from his father, from Abu al-Aswad, from 'Urwah, from 'A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her; and from his father, from 'Amr ibn Shu'ayb, from his father, from his grandfather, may Allah be pleased with them both: They both said: Whoever sleeps in any state in which he is not conscious must perform ablution."
"177","Muhammad ibn 'Umar narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us, from 'Umar ibn Abi Bakr ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith, from al-A'raj, who said: I saw Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, sleeping while sitting until I heard his snoring, then he would stand and pray without performing ablution."
"178","Abu Ya'la said: 'Abdullah ibn 'Amir narrated to us, Ibn Abi Za'idah narrated to us, from Hajjaj, who said: I mentioned to 'Ata' the sleep of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he snored then prayed, and he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was not like others."
"179","He said: 'Ubaydullah narrated to us, Khalid narrated to us, Sa'id narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, or from some of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that they used to lay their sides down, and he mentioned it."
"180","Ahmad ibn Mani' said: 'Abd al-Malik al-Tammar narrated to us, Abu Hilal narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: We used to come to the mosque of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to pray, and we would wait for the prayer; some of us dozed or slept, and he would not renew ablution. Hushaym said: This is not acted upon."
"181","Chapter on ablution after camel's milk: Ishaq said: al-Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman informed us, I heard Layth ibn Abi Sulaym narrating from a freedman of Musa ibn Talhah, or a son of Musa ibn Talhah, from his grandfather, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he used to perform ablution after camel's milk and its meat, and he would not pray in camel resting places."
"182","Ishaq said: al-Mu'tamir mentioned it to someone other than me, from his father, from his grandfather, meaning from Layth, from Musa, from his father, from his grandfather."
"183","I say: Thus al-Humaydi transmitted it, from al-Mu'tamir, with the wording: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I perform ablution after camel meat, and I do not pray in camel resting places."
"184","He also narrated it from al-Mu'tamir: I heard Layth narrating from a freedman of Musa ibn Talhah, or from a son of Musa ibn Talhah, from his father, from his grandfather Talhah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: One does not pray in camel resting places."
"185","Abu Ya'la said: Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn 'Ar'arah narrated to us, Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Layth, from a freedman of Musa ibn Talhah, or from a son of Musa ibn Talhah, from his father, from his grandfather, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to perform ablution after camel's milk and its meat, and would not pray in camel resting places; and he would not perform ablution after sheep's milk and its meat, and would pray in their resting places."
"186","Ibn Abi 'Umar said: Marwan, that is al-Fazari, narrated to us, from Aban, from Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to drink milk and not perform ablution after it, and drops would fall on his garment and he would not wash it."
"187","Abu Ya'la said: Abu 'Abd al-Rahman al-Adhrami narrated to us, 'Ubaydah ibn Humayd al-Dabbi informed us, from 'Abdullah ibn 'Abdullah, that is Abu Ja'far al-Razi, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Dhu al-Ghurrah, who said: A Bedouin met the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey and said: O Messenger of Allah, prayer catches us while we are in camel resting places, shall we pray? He said: No. He said: Shall we perform ablution after eating its meat? He said: Yes. He said: Shall we pray in sheep resting places? He said: Yes. He said: Shall we perform ablution after eating its meat? He said: No."
"188","Ishaq, that is Ibn Abi Isra'il, narrated to us, from 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn Muhammad, from 'Amr ibn Abi 'Amr, from 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Abdullah ibn 'Utbah, from Ibn Mas'ud, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) eating meat, then standing for prayer without touching a drop of water."
"189","Sulayman ibn 'Abd al-Jabbar Abu Ayyub narrated to us, Abu 'Asim narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from a man, from Mu'awiyah, may Allah be pleased with him, that he saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) eat dairy, then pray without performing ablution."
"190","Ibrahim ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri narrated to us, from Isra'il, from 'Abd al-A'la, from Muhammad ibn 'Ali, from 'Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to eat tharid and drink milk, then pray without performing ablution."
"191","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Husayn ibn 'Ali narrated to us, from Za'idah, from 'Abd al-'Aziz, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from 'Ikrimah, from 'A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would pass by the pot and take a bone with meat from it, eat some of it, then pray without performing ablution."
"192","Chapter on tayammum: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah said: 'Abbad ibn al-'Awwam narrated to us, from Burd, that is Ibn Sinan, from Sulayman ibn Musa, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: When the verse of tayammum was revealed, I did not know what to do, so I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to ask him but did not find him; I went seeking him and met him, and when he saw me he knew what I had come for, so he struck the earth with his hands and wiped his face. This is disconnected."
"193","Abu Ya'la said: Kamil ibn Talhah narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, 'Amr ibn Shu'ayb narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: Some men came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: We are people who stay in the sand, and major impurity, menstruation, and postnatal bleeding befall us, and we do not find water for four months? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Use the earth. It contains weakness."
"194","Shayban ibn Farrukh narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Rashid narrated to us, from 'Ata', from Ibn 'Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was on a journey, and when prayer time came the people stopped, and a shepherd saw them, so he stopped and struck the ground with his hand and performed tayammum, then called the adhan. The hadith contains weakness."
"195","Al-Harith said: Ashhal ibn Hatim narrated to us, 'Abdullah ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from 'Abdullah ibn Hubayrah, from Hanash, from Ibn 'Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pour out water and wipe himself with dust. I said to him: Water is close to you! He said: How do I know, perhaps I will not reach it. Weak."
"196","Musaddad said: Hushaym narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Harith, from 'Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: Tayammum is due at every prayer. Weak."
"197","Abu Ya'la said: 'Ubaydullah al-Qawariri narrated to us, Jarir ibn 'Abd al-Hamid narrated to us, from Qabus, that is Ibn Abi Zibyan, from his father, from Ibn 'Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: The best earth is the plowed land. Stopped, fair."
"198","Book of ritual bathing. Chapter on covering during bathing: Abu Bakr said: al-Fadl ibn Dukayn narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, from Jabir, from Sa'd ibn 'Ubaydah, from Silah ibn Zufar, from Hudhayfah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: I stood with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a night of Ramadan, and he stood to bathe and I screened him, and some leftover of his remained in the vessel, and he said: If you wish, pour it away, and if you wish, pour more upon it. I said: O Messenger of Allah, this leftover is dearer to me than what I would pour upon it. He said: So I bathed with it, and he screened me. I said: Do not screen me! He said: Rather, I screened you as you screened me. Jabir, that is al-Ju'fi, is weak."
"199","Al-Harith said: 'Umar ibn Sa'id ibn Masruq narrated to us, from his father, from Makhul, from Muhammad ibn Suwayd al-Fihri, from Hudhayfah, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he mentioned it at length."
"200","Musaddad said: Yahya narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, 'Ata' narrated to me, Safwan ibn Ya'la informed me, from his father, who said: While 'Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, was bathing beside a camel, meaning while in ihram, and I was screening him with a garment, he said to me: O Ya'la, pour water on my head! I said: The Commander of the Faithful knows best. He said: By Allah, I do not see water increasing the hair except in dishevelment. He said: In the name of Allah, and he poured over his head."
"201","Chapter on one who warms himself with his wife after bathing: Musaddad said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from al-Zubayr ibn al-Khirrit, from 'Ikrimah, may Allah be pleased with him, that he saw no harm in a man bathing from major impurity and then warming himself with his wife before she bathes, or the woman bathing before the man and then warming herself with him."
"202","Abu 'Awanah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, who said: 'Amir said to Ibrahim: What do you say about one who bathes from major impurity then warms himself with his wife? He said: I do not know. He said: Shall I not inform you about your friend 'Alqamah that he saw no harm in it."
"203","Hushaym narrated to us, from Mughirah, from Ibrahim, that he saw no harm in that."
"204","Chapter on the description of bathing: Musaddad said: 'Abdullah narrated to us, from Fudayl, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, that when he bathed he sprinkled his eyes with water and inserted his finger into his navel. Authentic as a stopped report. Malik narrated it from Nafi', and it was narrated raised but it is not authentic."
"205","Abu Dawud said: Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us, from Shu'bah, who said: Ibn 'Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, when he bathed from major impurity would pour with his right over his left seven times."
"206","Musaddad said: Yahya narrated to us, from Mis'ar ibn Kidam, Bukayr ibn al-Akhnas narrated to me, al-Ma'rur narrated to me, who said: 'Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, said: As for me, I pour over my head three handfuls."
"207","Abu Bakr said: Waki' narrated to us, Fudayl ibn Marzuq narrated to us, from 'Atiyyah, from Abu Sa'id, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: A man asked him about bathing from major impurity, and he said: Three times. The man said: I have abundant hair? He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had more hair than you and better."
"208","Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Humayd al-Tawil, from Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The delegation of Thaqif said: O Messenger of Allah, our land is a cold land, so what suffices us of bathing from major impurity? He said: As for me, I pour over my head three times."
"209","Abu Ya'la said: Ibn Abi Saminah narrated to us, Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us with it. Authentic."
"210","Abu Musa Ishaq ibn Musa al-Khatmi al-Ansari narrated to us, 'Asim ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Zayd ibn Qunfudh narrated to us, from Jabir ibn Saylan, from Ibn Mas'ud, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: A man asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about a man who bathes from major impurity but water misses part of his body, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He washes that place, then prays."
"211","Ishaq said: al-Muqri' informed us, Sa'id ibn Abi Ayyub narrated to us, Yazid ibn Abi Habib narrated to us, from Na'im, freedman of Umm Salamah: I asked Umm Salamah about a man's bathing, and she said: He cleans the hair and saturates the skin. And I asked her about a woman's bathing, and she said: She cleans her forelock and does not undo her head."
"212","Chapter on the bathhouse and dislike of nudity: Musaddad said: Yahya narrated to us, from Sufyan, from 'Umarah ibn al-Qa'qa', from Abu Zur'ah, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: What a fine house is the bathhouse; it removes dirt and reminds of the Fire. Authentic as a stopped report."
"213","Ahmad ibn Mani' said: 'Ammar ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Yahya ibn 'Ubaydullah, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What a fine house is the bathhouse; the Muslim man enters it, for when he enters it he asks Allah Almighty for Paradise and seeks refuge with Him from the Fire. And what an evil house is the wedding feast; the Muslim man enters it, for when he enters it, it makes him desire the world and makes him forget the Hereafter."
"214","Ibn Abi 'Umar said: al-Muqri' narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi Ayyub narrated to us, Abu Khayrah informed me, from Musa ibn Wardan; Abu Khayrah said: I know it only from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him not enter the bathhouse except with a waistcloth, and whoever among the females of my nation believes in Allah and the Last Day, let her not enter the bathhouse."
"215","Musaddad said: 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, 'Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, who said: I asked Muhammad ibn Sirin about entering the bathhouse, and he said: 'Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, used to dislike it."
"216","Hushaym narrated to us, from Mansur ibn Zadhdhan, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, who said: Ibn 'Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, would not enter the bathhouse, saying: It is among the luxuries they introduced."
"217","Hushaym narrated to us, from Mansur, from al-Hasan and Muhammad, that they would not enter the bathhouse."
"218","'Abdullah, that is Ibn Dawud, narrated to us, from Mis'ar, from 'Atiyyah, from Ibn 'Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, that he would enter the bathhouse and the bathhouse attendant would apply depilatory to him; when he reached his waist, he told the bathhouse attendant: Go out."
"219","Abu Ya'la said: 'Abd al-A'la narrated to us, Hammad ibn Shu'ayb narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade entering water except with a waistcloth."
"220","Abu Bakr ibn Zanjawayh narrated to us, 'Amr ibn al-Rabi' ibn Tariq narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to me, from Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim, from Muhammad ibn Thabit ibn Shurahbil, from 'Abdullah ibn Suwayd al-Khatmi, from Abu Ayyub al-Ansari, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him honor his neighbor; and whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him honor his guest; and whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him say good or keep silent; and whoever among your women believes in Allah and the Last Day, let them not enter the bathhouse. He said: So I mentioned it to 'Umar ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz, may Allah be pleased with him, during his caliphate, and he wrote to Abu Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn 'Amr ibn Hazm to ask Muhammad ibn Thabit about his hadith, for he is pleasing, so he asked him and wrote to 'Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, and he barred women from the bathhouse. Ibn Hibban and al-Hakim authenticated it."
"221","Chapter on commanding the one in major impurity to bathe when he wants to return: Ishaq and Musaddad said: al-Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman informed us, from Layth ibn Abi Sulaym, from 'Asim, from Abu al-Mushma'il, from 'Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: When one of you comes to his wife and wants to return, let him wash his private part."
"222","Abu Ya'la said: 'Ubaydullah, that is al-Qawariri, narrated to us, Mu'tamir narrated to us with it."
"223","Chapter on preventing the one in major impurity from entering the mosque: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah said: al-Fadl ibn Dukayn narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Ghaniyyah, from Abu al-Khattab, from Mahduj al-Hudhali, from Jasrah: Umm Salamah, may Allah be pleased with her, narrated to me, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to the courtyard of the mosque and called at the top of his voice: This mosque is not lawful for one in major impurity nor for a menstruating woman, except for the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his wives and 'Ali and Fatimah, may Allah be pleased with them; have I not made the names clear to you lest you go astray? Ibn Majah transmitted it from Abu Bakr, without his saying: Except for the Prophet to the end."
"224","Chapter on commanding the one in major impurity to perform ablution if he does not bathe: Musaddad said: Yahya narrated to us, Mis'ar narrated to us, Bukayr ibn al-Akhnas narrated to me, from Mus'ab ibn Sa'd, who said: Sa'd, may Allah be pleased with him, would become impure then perform ablution and go out."
"225","Chapter on disagreement over the purity of semen: Musaddad said: Yahya narrated to us, from Shu'bah, from Mansur, from Mujahid, from Mus'ab ibn Sa'd, from Sa'd, may Allah be pleased with him, that he used to scrape semen from his garment."
"226","Yahya narrated to us, from Shu'bah, an elder narrated to me that he heard Ibn 'Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, say about a man who has a wet dream in a garment and it is hidden from him: Wash the whole garment."
"227","Chapter on making bathing obligatory by the meeting of the two circumcised parts, and abrogation of the saying: Water is from water: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah said: 'Abd al-A'la narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Ma'mar ibn Abi Huyayyah, freedman of the daughter of Safwan, from 'Ubayd ibn Rifa'ah ibn Rafi', from his father Rifa'ah ibn Rafi', who said: 'Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, gave a ruling concerning Rifa'ah, saying: Did you used to do that, when one of you had intercourse with a woman then was sluggish, he did not bathe? He said: We used to do that in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and no prohibition came to us from Allah Almighty about it, nor was there any prohibition from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about it."
"228","Imam Ahmad narrated it, saying: Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Zuhayr and Ibn Idris narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Ma'mar ibn Abi Huyayyah, from 'Ubayd ibn Rifa'ah ibn Rafi', from his father, Zuhayr said in his hadith: Rifa'ah ibn Rafi', and he was an 'Aqabi Badri, who said: I was with 'Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, when it was said to him: Zayd ibn Thabit, may Allah be pleased with him, is giving people rulings in the mosque, Zuhayr said in his hadith: People by his opinion, about one who has intercourse and does not emit, so he said: Bring him quickly, and he was brought. He said: O enemy of yourself, have you reached the point of giving people rulings in the mosque of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) by your opinion? He said: I did not do that; my paternal uncles narrated to me from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: Which of your uncles? He said: Ubayy ibn Ka'b. Zuhayr said: And Abu Ayyub, and Rifa'ah ibn Rafi'. 'Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, turned to me and said: What does this youth say? I said: We used to do it in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: Did you ask the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about it? He said: We used to do it in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: So he gathered the people, and they agreed that water is only from water, except for two men: 'Ali ibn Abi Talib and Mu'adh ibn Jabal, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: When the circumcised part passes the circumcised part, bathing is obligatory. He said: So 'Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said: O Commander of the Faithful, the most knowledgeable of people about this are the wives of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)! So he sent to Hafsah, may Allah be pleased with her, and she said: I have no knowledge. So he sent to 'A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, and she said: When the circumcised part passes the circumcised part, bathing is obligatory. So 'Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, was crushed, then said: It shall not reach me that anyone does it without bathing except that I punish him severely."
"229","'Abdullah ibn Ahmad said: 'Abdullah ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me, 'Abd al-A'la narrated to us, and he mentioned it at length. And Ma'mar was declared trustworthy by Ibn Ma'in. Its origin is in the Sahih without this context, and some of them narrated the hadith of 'A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, alone."
"230","Ahmad ibn Mani' said: Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Layth ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Ma'mar ibn Abi Huyayyah, from 'Ubayd ibn Rifa'ah, from Zayd ibn Thabit, may Allah be pleased with him, that he used to preach, saying in his sermons: If a man mixes with a woman and does not emit, there is no bathing upon him. So a man stood from Zayd's presence and came to 'Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, and informed him, and 'Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, said to the man: Go to him and bring him to me, so that you may be a witness against him! When he came to him, 'Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, said to him: O enemy of Allah, are you the one who misleads people without knowledge! Zayd, may Allah be pleased with him, said: By Allah, O Commander of the Faithful, I did not invent it on my own; my paternal uncles informed me of it. He said: And which of your uncles? He said: Ubayy, Abu Ayyub, and Rifa'ah, then in the presence of 'Umar, may Allah be pleased with them, and Rifa'ah, may Allah be pleased with him, said: O Commander of the Faithful, we used to do it in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And he said: And did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) know? He said: I have no knowledge. So 'Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said to him: O Commander of the Faithful, this matter is not sound; and Mu'adh, may Allah be pleased with him, said to him: O Commander of the Faithful, this matter is not sound."
"231","Chapter: Water is from water: Musaddad: Yahya narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, Mansur narrated to me, from Hilal ibn Yasaf, from Kharashah ibn Habib, from 'Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: A man said to him: A man comes to his wife without emitting? He said: Even if he shook her until his temples shake, there is no bathing upon him."
"232","And from Sufyan, Sulayman narrated to me, from Ibrahim, from 'Alqamah, from 'Abdullah."
"233","And from Sufyan, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from 'Abdullah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: Had I reached that from her, I would have bathed."
"234","'Abdullah ibn Dawud narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, I think from 'Alqamah; al-A'mash doubted in it."
"235","Yahya narrated to us, from Sufyan and Shu'bah, from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim al-Taymi, from his father, who said: I heard 'Abdullah, may Allah be pleased with him, say: Water is from water, and there is no harm in one dirham and two dirhams."
"236","Yahya narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from 'Ata', who said: I heard Ibn 'Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, say: Water is from water. Authentic as a stopped report."
"237","Abu Ya'la said: 'Abdullah ibn 'Umar ibn Aban narrated to us, Talhah ibn Sinan narrated to us, from Abu Sa'd, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent to a man of the Ansar, and he was late, so he said: What detained you? He said: When your messenger came to me I was with my wife, so I stood and bathed, and he said: No harm on you not to bathe so long as you do not emit. He said: So the Ansar used to do that. Abu Sa'd is Sa'id ibn al-Marzuban al-Baqqal, weak."
"238","Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, Zayd ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Abu Salamah ibn 'Abd al-Rahman, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went seeking a man of the Ansar and called him, and the Ansari came out with his head dripping water, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What alarmed you? He said: You called me while I was with my wife, and I feared delaying you, so I hastened and poured water over me, then came out, and he said: Had you emitted? He said: No. He said: If you do that, then do not bathe; wash what touched the woman of you, and perform your ablution for prayer, for water is from water."
"239","Chapter on bathing after a wet dream: Abu Bakr said: Muhammad ibn Bishr al-'Abdi narrated to us, 'Abdullah ibn al-Mu'ammal narrated to us, from 'Amr ibn Shu'ayb, from his father, from his grandfather, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: A woman called Busrah came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, one of us sees that she is with her husband in a dream? He said: If you find wetness, then bathe, O Busrah. He said: So 'A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, said to her: You have exposed women! He said: Leave her to ask about whatever occurs to her; dust be on your forehead, or dust be on your right hand."
"240","Ishaq said: 'Ubaydullah ibn Musa informed us, Isra'il narrated to us, from 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn Rufay', from Abu Salamah: Umm Sulaym, mother of Anas ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with them both, narrated to me, saying: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, one of us sees in her dream what a man sees? He said: Does she feel desire? She said: Perhaps. He said: Does she find water? She said: Perhaps. He said: Then let her bathe. This is an authentic chain, but it has a defect."
"241","Ishaq said: Jarir informed us, from 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn Rufay', from Abu Salamah ibn 'Abd al-Rahman, 'Ata', and Mujahid, who said: Umm Sulaym, may Allah be pleased with her, asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he mentioned something similar, saying wetness instead of water. And he said at its end: He said: If she sees that, let her bathe. Women met her and said to her: You have exposed us before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)! She said: I would not stop until I know whether I am in lawful or unlawful! I say: The origin of this hadith is with al-Nasa'i through Sa'id, from Qatadah, from Anas, from Umm Sulaym, may Allah be pleased with them both. And Muslim transmitted it through another chain from Sa'id, but the apparent context is that it is from the Musnad of Anas, may Allah be pleased with him. And the origin of the story is in the two Sahihs through Zaynab bint Umm Salamah, from Umm Salamah, who said: Umm Sulaym, may Allah be pleased with her, came."
"242","Ishaq said: Muhammad ibn Bakr informed us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, Ibn Khuthaym informed me, that Sulayman ibn 'Atiq informed him that a woman came to Umm Sulaym and said: I saw as if so-and-so is marrying me, and Umm Salamah mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: If she sees moisture, let her bathe."
"243","Chapter on obligatory and recommended baths: Musaddad said: 'Abdullah ibn Dawud narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, from Mujahid, from 'Abdullah ibn 'Amr, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: Bathing is for five: cupping, the bathhouse, major impurity, the dead, and Friday. He said: So that was mentioned to Ibrahim, and he said: They did not count any bathing as obligatory except major impurity, and they used to recommend the Friday bath."
"244","Yahya narrated to us, Hisham ibn 'Urwah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from 'A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, who said: If one of you is in major impurity, let him not sleep, for he does not know; perhaps his soul may be taken in his sleep."
"245","Book of menstruation. Chapter on the beginning of menstruation: Ahmad ibn Mani' said: 'Abbad ibn al-'Awwam narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Husayn narrated to us, from Ya'la ibn Muslim, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: Allah, Blessed and Exalted, said to Adam: O Adam, what carried you to eat from the tree I forbade you? Adam made an excuse, saying: O Lord, Hawwa' made it attractive to me. He said: I have punished her by making her carry only with hardship, deliver only with hardship, and making her bleed twice every month. He said: So Hawwa' wailed at that, and it was said to her: Upon you is the wailing, and upon your daughters. This is stopped, with an authentic chain."
"246","Chapter on the purity of a menstruating woman's body: Ishaq said: al-Mula'i informed us, Salih ibn Rustum narrated to us, from Abu Yazid al-Madani, who said: Umm Ayman said: He said: Hand me the mat. It was said: Who? He said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). She said: I am menstruating. He said: Your menstruation is not in your hand."
"247","Chapter on disliking looking at menstrual blood at night: Musaddad said: Isma'il narrated to us, 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq informed us, from 'Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr, from 'Amrah bint 'Abd al-Rahman, who said: 'A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, used to forbid women from looking at themselves at night during menstruation, saying: Yellowish and turbid discharge may occur."
"248","Ishaq said: Ibn 'Ulayyah informed us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Fatimah bint al-Mundhir narrated to me, saying: Asma' and her brother's daughters used to narrate to us; one of us would bathe after purity then menstruation, its flow continuing to yellowish and turbid discharge, and she would command us to abstain from prayer until we see only pure white."
"249","Ishaq said: al-Mula'i, that is Abu Nu'aym, informed us, Mis'ar narrated to us, from Abu Bakr ibn 'Umarah, from a Qurayshi woman, from Umm Salamah, may Allah be pleased with her, who said: One of us would bathe and her yellowness would remain."
"250","Chapter on the woman with prolonged bleeding: Abu Ya'la said: al-Hasan ibn 'Umar ibn Shaqiq narrated to us, Ja'far ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: Fatimah bint Qays, may Allah be pleased with her, asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the woman with prolonged bleeding, and he said: Count the days of your periods. And he commanded her to use a pad, pray, and bathe for every period of purity."
"251","Abu Hammam narrated to us, 'Abd al-A'la narrated to us, al-Jald ibn Ayyub narrated to us, from Mu'awiyah ibn Qurrah, from Anas ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: Let her observe five, seven, eight, nine, ten; when ten pass, she is a woman with prolonged bleeding."
"252","Ishaq said: Jarir informed us, from Layth, from Muhammad ibn Shihab, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded Umm Habibah to bathe at every prayer, and she had experienced prolonged bleeding. I say: Layth is weak, and Umm Habibah is the daughter of Jahsh, and the origin of the hadith about her is in the Sunan, connected."
"253","Chapter on forbidding intercourse with a menstruating woman, its expiation, and what is permitted of her: Ibn Abi 'Umar said: al-Muqri' narrated to us, from al-Ifriqi, 'Umarah ibn Ghurab narrated to me, saying: A paternal aunt of his narrated to him that she asked 'A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, saying: One of us menstruates and she and her husband have only one bed and one blanket, so what should she do? She said: She ties her waistcloth over herself, then sleeps with him, and for him is what is above that. Weak."
"254","Musaddad said: Yahya narrated to us, from 'Umar ibn Dharr, Hanzalah ibn Sabrah ibn al-Musayyib ibn Najabah narrated to me, from his paternal aunt Jumanah, who was under Hudhayfah, who said: Hudhayfah, may Allah be pleased with him, would return from the dawn prayer in Ramadan and enter with her into her blanket, turning his back to her and not facing her, meaning while she was menstruating. Stopped, fair."
"255","Ishaq said: Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid informed us, al-Awza'i narrated to us, Yazid ibn Abi Malik narrated to me, from Ibn Zayd ibn al-Khattab, from 'Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, that he had a wife who disliked men, and whenever he wanted her she claimed menstruation, so he thought she was lying and came to her and found her truthful, then he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he commanded him to give a fifth of a dinar in charity. A fair hadith."
"256","And 'Isa ibn Yunus informed us, Zayd ibn 'Abd al-Hamid, of the offspring of Zayd ibn al-Khattab, narrated to us, from his father, who said: 'Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, had a wife, and he mentioned something similar."
"257","Al-Harith said: al-Hakam ibn Musa narrated to us, 'Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, and he mentioned it, but his wording: 'Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, came to a slave girl of his, and she said: I am menstruating, but he had intercourse with her and found her menstruating, so he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned that to him, and he said: May Allah forgive you, O Abu Hafs, give half a dinar in charity."
"258","Book of prayer. Chapter on the virtue of prayer: Musaddad said: Hammad narrated to us, from Abu Qilabah, who said: 'Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, came upon Mu'adh, may Allah be pleased with him, while he was among some of his companions, and said: O Mu'adh, what sustains this affair? He said: Sincerity, which is the natural disposition; prayer, which is the creed; and obedience."
"259","Ishaq said: al-Nadr informed us, Hammad, that is Ibn Salamah, narrated to us, Ma'bad informed us, so-and-so informed us, while he was in the mosque of Damascus, from 'Awf ibn Malik, who said: Abu Dharr, may Allah be pleased with him, sat with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he mentioned the hadith like a previous hadith. He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, what is prayer? He said: A good thing laid down; whoever wishes does less of it, and whoever wishes does more."
"260","Musaddad: Bishr, that is Ibn al-Mufaddal, narrated to us, Muhajir Abu Makhlad narrated to us, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The first thing the servant is judged by is his purification; if he perfects his purification, his prayer is like his purification, then he is judged by his prayer; if his prayer is good, the rest of his deeds are like his prayer."
"261","Abu Bakr said: Bakr ibn 'Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, 'Isa, that is Ibn al-Mukhtar, narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Layla narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: What of a man who recites at the beginning of the night then steals at its end? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If he recites at its beginning, its end prevents him from stealing in the darkness."
"262","Chapter on the greatness of prayer: Ahmad ibn Mani' said: al-Hasan ibn Sawwar Abu al-'Ala' narrated to us, al-Layth ibn Sa'd narrated to us, Mu'awiyah ibn Salih narrated to us, saying: Abu 'Abd al-Rahman al-Azdi narrated to him, saying: I heard Ibn 'A'idh say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out in the funeral of a man of the Ansar, and he mentioned the hadith, and in it: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O 'Umar, you are not asked about people's deeds, but you are asked about prayer."
"263","Abu Ya'la said: Harun ibn Ma'ruf narrated to us, Isma'il ibn 'Ayyash narrated to us, Bahir ibn Sa'd al-Kala'i narrated to us, from Khalid ibn Ma'dan, from Abu 'Atiyyah, who said: A man died in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And he mentioned it in full. It will come, God willing, in funerals."
"264","Al-Harith said: Ishaq narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Yazid al-Raqashi, from Anas ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The first thing the servant is judged by is his prayer; Allah, Blessed and Exalted, says to the angels: Look at My servant's prayer; if they find it complete, it is written for him complete, and if they find something diminished from it, He says: See whether you find voluntary prayers for My servant, so his prayer is completed from his voluntary prayers, then deeds are taken in like measure. With this or similar."
"265","Abu Ya'la said: Abu al-Rabi' al-Zahrani narrated to us, Hammad, that is Ibn Zayd, narrated to us with it, fuller, and its beginning: The first thing Allah Almighty obligated upon people of their religion is prayer, and the last that remains is prayer, and the first they are judged by is prayer. He says: Look at My servant's prayer, and he mentioned it until he said: If voluntary prayer is found for him, the obligatory is completed from the voluntary. Then he said: See whether his zakah is complete; if his zakah is found complete, it is written complete, and if found deficient, He says: See whether he has charity; if he has, his zakah is completed from the charity."
"266","Abu Ya'la said: Sufyan ibn Waki' narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Isma'il al-Ansari, Salih ibn Kaysan narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Marwan al-Aslami, from his father, from his grandfather, who said: We came to Abu Dharr, may Allah be pleased with him, six persons, the sixth a man of Juhaynah, and we of Aslam, and found him departing, leaving Madinah. He said: Welcome to you; what brought you? They said: We came to greet you and learn from you. He said: Yes, I heard Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The five prayers, whoever meets Allah Almighty with them without diminishing anything of them, Allah forgives his sins even if they fill the earth. We said: What of what passed in ignorance? He said: Piety wipes it, twice. The Juhani said to him: Did you hear this from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Glory be to Allah, is it lawful for a man to lie upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)?!"
"267","Abu Bakr said: Muhammad ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, Kathir ibn 'Abdullah, that is al-Ubulli, narrated to us, from Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: O Anas, if you can always pray, for the angels pray upon you as long as you pray."
"268","Al-Harith said: al-Hasan ibn Qutaybah narrated to us, Sufyan al-Thawri narrated to us, from Mansur, from Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd, from Ibn 'Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Be upright, and you will never encompass; know that the best of your deeds is prayer, and none preserves ablution except a believer. I say: This is inverted; the preserved is from Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd, from Thawban, may Allah be pleased with him. Hadith of Maymunah, may Allah be pleased with her: Nothing draws My servant near to Me like performing My obligation, will come, God willing, in voluntary prayer."
"269","Ahmad ibn Mani' said: 'Abd al-Malik ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us. And 'Abd ibn Humayd said: al-Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us. Both said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from 'Ali ibn Zayd, from Yusuf ibn Mihran, from Ibn 'Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Jibril, peace be upon him, said to me: Prayer has been made beloved to you, so take from it what you wish."
"270","Al-Harith said: Ishaq narrated to us, Abu al-Ashhab narrated to us, from al-Hasan, raised: The five prayers, and Friday to Friday, are expiations for what is between them so long as major sins are avoided."
"271","Abu Ya'la said: Zakariyya ibn Yahya narrated to us, Dawud ibn al-Zibriqan narrated to us, from 'Ali ibn Zayd, from Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The likeness of the five prayers is like a sweet flowing river, or deep water, at one's door, from which he bathes five times every day; what would remain of his dirt?"
"272","Ishaq ibn Abi Isra'il narrated to us, Hatim ibn Isma'il narrated to us, from Humayd ibn Sakhr, from Yazid al-Raqashi, from Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever prays the dawn prayer and his covenant is violated, the sanctuary of Allah Almighty has been violated, his covenant broken, and I am the claimant of his covenant."
"273","Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, 'Abd al-Malik ibn Nusayr, freedman of Marwan ibn al-Hakam, narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Isma'il al-Ansari narrated to us, from Yunus Abu 'Imran ibn Anas, from his grandmother Umm Anas, may Allah be pleased with them both, that she said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I said to him: May Allah place you in the highest companionship of Paradise, and me with you. He said: Amen. I said: O Messenger of Allah, teach me a righteous deed to do? He said: Establish prayer, for it is the best jihad; abandon sins, for it is the best emigration; and remember Allah much, for the most beloved of deeds to Allah, Blessed and Exalted, is to meet Him with it."
"274","Chapter on the adhan: Ishaq said: Jarir informed us, from al-Mughirah, from al-Sha'bi, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was concerned about the call for prayer, and disliked striking a clapper as the people of Mecca do, so he used to send men when prayer came and it distracted them from prayer. And 'Abdullah ibn Zayd al-Ansari, may Allah be pleased with him, returned, concerned with the concern of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he was visited in sleep, and it was said: Why are you concerned? He said: For the concern of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The one who came to him said: Come to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and command him to call for prayer: Allah is Greatest, Allah is Greatest, Allah is Greatest, Allah is Greatest; I bear witness there is no god but Allah, twice; I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, twice; come to prayer, twice; come to success, twice; Allah is Greatest, Allah is Greatest; there is no god but Allah. Then he said to him: Make between the adhan and the iqamah the like of that. He said: So 'Abdullah, may Allah be pleased with him, came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him of that, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Teach it to Bilal. And 'Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, came and said: I saw the like of what 'Abdullah ibn Zayd saw, but 'Abdullah preceded me. This is mursal, with an authentic chain, and it is a good witness for the hadith of Ibn Ishaq transmitted in the Sunan."
"275","Abu Ya'la said: Zuhayr ibn Harb narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Makhzumi narrated to us, Usamah ibn Zayd ibn Aslam informed me, from his father, from his grandfather, from 'Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: Abu Mahdhurah, may Allah be pleased with him, called the noon adhan, while 'Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, was in Mecca, and raised his voice when the sun declined, so 'Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, said: O Abu Mahdhurah, did you not fear your uvula would split? He said: I wanted you to hear me. So 'Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Delay prayer when heat is intense, for heat is from the exhalation of Hell; Hell disputed until parts of it ate parts of it, so it sought permission from Allah, Blessed and Exalted, for two breaths and He permitted it; the severity of heat is from the exhalation of Hell, and the severity of bitter cold is from its cold."
"276","Al-Bazzar narrated it, saying: al-Fadl ibn Sahl and Ahmad ibn al-Walid narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Makhzumi narrated to us with it, saying: We know it not raised from 'Umar except through this chain, and Muhammad ibn al-Hasan is rejected in hadith."
"277","Al-Harith said: Dawud ibn Rushayd narrated to us, Abu Haywah narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Sinan narrated to us, from Abu al-Zahiriyyah, from Kathir ibn Murrah al-Hadrami, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The first who called the adhan in heaven is Jibril, peace be upon him. So 'Umar and Bilal, may Allah be pleased with them both, heard it; 'Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, came and informed the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) of what he heard, then Bilal, may Allah be pleased with him, came and informed the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) of what he heard, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: 'Umar preceded you, O Bilal; call as you heard. He said: Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded him to place his fingers in his ears, seeking aid with them for the voice."
"278","Chapter on the muezzin of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): al-Harith said: Rawh ibn 'Ubadah narrated to us, Musa ibn 'Ubaydah narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had two muezzins, one Bilal, and the other 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn al-Asamm, may Allah be pleased with them both."
"279","Abu Nu'aym said: Abu Bakr ibn Khallad narrated to us, al-Harith narrated to us with it. Abu Qurrah al-Zubaydi narrated it in his Sunan through Musa ibn 'Ubaydah likewise, adding: Bilal, may Allah be pleased with him, used to call at night to wake the sleeper, and Ibn Umm Maktum, may Allah be pleased with him, used to aim for dawn and not miss it; as if 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn al-Asamm, may Allah be pleased with him, on this basis is Ibn Umm Maktum, and Allah knows best."
"280","Chapter on the description of the adhan and its place: al-Harith said: Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah narrated to us, Hisham ibn 'Urwah narrated to us, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, that he used to call the adhan in pairs and make the iqamah odd."
"281","Musaddad said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, or from others of the people of Mecca, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded Bilal, may Allah be pleased with him, to call the adhan atop the Ka'bah."
"282","Chapter on calling before dawn in Ramadan: Ishaq said: Ahmad ibn Ayyub informed us, from Abu Hamzah al-Sukkari, from Jabir, from Abu Nasr, who said: Bilal, may Allah be pleased with him, said: I called at night, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You have prevented people from food and drink; go and ascend and call: The servant has slept. So I went, saying of Bilal, and called three times: The servant has slept. This is a weak chain with a break."
"283","Al-Harith said: Dawud ibn al-Muhabbar narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Hisham ibn 'Urwah, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not rely on the adhan of Ibn Umm Maktum, but on the adhan of Bilal. And Ibn Umm Maktum was blind. Mursal."
"284","Chapter on the imam not being a muezzin: Musaddad said: 'Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid narrated to us, from Qays, that is Ibn Abi Hazim, who said: 'Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, said: Had I capacity for the adhan along with the caliphate, I would have called. Authentic."
"285","'Isa narrated to us, Isma'il informed us from Shubayl ibn 'Awf, who said: 'Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, said to his companions: Who is your muezzin? They said: Our slaves and freedmen. He said: Our freedmen and slaves; that is a great deficiency for you."
"286","Chapter on the virtue of muezzins: 'Abd ibn Humayd said: 'Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ma'mar informed us, from Aban, from al-'Ala' ibn Ziyad, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The most beloved of Allah's servants to Allah Almighty are those who observe the sun and the moon. Hadith of Bilal, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Nothing is better than your deed except jihad, will come, God willing, in the virtue of jihad."
"287","Ibn Abi 'Umar said: al-Muqri' narrated to us, al-Ifriqi narrated to us, Salman ibn 'Amir al-Sha'bani narrated to us, from Abu 'Uthman al-Asbahi, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: The muezzin's merit over one present at prayer by his adhan is one hundred twenty; if he calls the iqamah, then two hundred forty good deeds, except one who says like his saying."
"288","Al-Harith said: Sa'id ibn Shurahbil narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Abu al-Khayr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Muezzins are the longest-necked of people on the Day of Resurrection, and they are the first to be permitted to speak on the Day of Resurrection. Mursal. Al-Tabarani transmitted it in al-Awsat through another chain from Ibn Lahi'ah with this chain to Abu al-Khayr, from 'Uqbah ibn 'Amir, connected."
"289","Abu Ya'la said: Ahmad ibn Janab narrated to us, 'Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, from 'Ubaydullah ibn al-Walid, from Muharib, from Ibn 'Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The people of heaven hear nothing from the people of earth except the adhan. 'Ubaydullah is very weak."
"290","Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Shami narrated to us, in 'Abbadan, Muhammad ibn al-'Ala' al-Ayli narrated to me, from Yunus ibn Yazid, from al-Zuhri, from Anas, from Ubayy ibn Ka'b, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was admitted to Paradise and saw in it domes of pearl, so I said: Whose is this, O Jibril? He said: For the muezzins and imams of your nation. Muhammad, the shaykh of Abu Ya'la, is very weak."
"291","Ishaq, that is Ibn Abi Isra'il, narrated to us: Abda narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Muslim, from al-Hasan who said: It has reached us that the first of people to be clothed on the Day of Resurrection from the garments of Paradise are the mu'adhdhins."
"292","Chapter: what one says when he hears the mu'adhdhin. Ahmad ibn Mani' said: al-Nadr ibn Isma'il narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, from Abd Allah ibn Ukaym, who said: Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, when he heard the adhan would say: Welcome to those who speak justly, and welcome to the prayer and its people."
"293","And he also said: al-Nadr ibn Isma'il narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, from al-Nu'man ibn Sa'd, who said: Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, when he heard the adhan would say: Let every witness bear witness to it, and I take it upon myself against every denier."
"294","Abu Ya'la said: al-Hakam ibn Musa narrated to us: al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Abu A'idh, that is Ufayr ibn Mi'dan, from Sulaym ibn Amir, from Abu Umama, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who said: When the caller calls to prayer the gates of heaven are opened and supplication is answered; so whoever is struck by distress or hardship should watch for the caller: when he says Allahu Akbar he says Allahu Akbar, when he testifies he testifies, when he says come to prayer he says come to prayer, when he says come to success he says come to success, then he says: O Allah, Lord of this perfect call, the call of truth that is answered and granted, the call of truth and the word of piety, keep us alive upon it, cause us to die upon it, resurrect us upon it, and make us among the best of its people in our life and death; then he asks Allah for his need. Al-Tabarani brought it at length in al-Du'a from Abd Allah ibn Ahmad from al-Hakam ibn Musa, and al-Hakim brought it at length in al-Mustadrak by way of al-Haytham ibn Kharija from al-Walid."
"295","And Ahmad ibn Mani' brought it from al-Haytham up to his saying: and supplication is answered, and he did not mention what came after it."
"296","Al-Harith said: Dawud ibn al-Muhabbar narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from a man of Banu Hashim, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who said, like a previous hadith: When the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, heard the mu'adhdhin saying Allahu Akbar, Allahu Akbar, he would say the like of what he says; when he said I bear witness there is no god but Allah, he would say the like; when he said I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, he would say the like of what he says; and when he said come to prayer, come to success, he would say: there is no power nor strength except with Allah. In it is weakness and a break in the chain."
"297","Abu Ya'la said: Abu al-Rabi' narrated to us: Sallam narrated to us, from Zayd al-Ammi, from Yazid al-Raqashi, from Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, camped one night and Bilal, may Allah be pleased with him, gave the adhan, and he said: Whoever says the like of his saying and bears the like of his testimony, for him is Paradise. Its chain is weak."
"298","Chapter: the merit of one who gives adhan seeking reward. Al-Harith: Dawud ibn al-Muhabbar narrated to us: Maysara ibn Abd Rabbih narrated to us, from Abu A'isha al-Sa'di, from Yazid ibn Umar, from Abu Salama ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurayra and Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them, who both said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, addressed us and said: Whoever undertakes the adhan of a mosque among the mosques of Allah the Exalted seeking thereby the Face of Allah, mighty and majestic, Allah the Exalted gives him the reward of forty thousand thousand prophets, and forty thousand thousand truthful ones, and forty thousand thousand martyrs, and forty thousand thousand communities enter into his intercession, in every community forty thousand thousand men, and for him in every part of the Gardens are forty thousand thousand abodes, in every abode forty thousand thousand houses, in every house forty thousand thousand beds, upon every bed a wife from the wide-eyed maidens, the expanse of every house thereof the expanse of the world forty thousand thousand times, before every wife forty thousand thousand maidservants, in every house forty thousand thousand tables, upon every table forty thousand thousand bowls, in every bowl forty thousand thousand kinds; if the two heavy beings came to him the least of his houses would suffice them with whatever they wish of food, drink, clothing, perfume, fruits, and kinds of gifts, rarities, ornaments and robes, every house thereof self-sufficient with what is in it of these things from the other house. Then when the mu'adhdhin says I bear witness there is no god but Allah, seventy thousand thousand angels surround him, all of them praying for him and seeking forgiveness for him, and he is in the shade of Allah's mercy, mighty and majestic, until he finishes, and forty thousand thousand angels write his reward for him, then they ascend with it to Allah the Exalted. This is fabricated; Maysara ibn Abd Rabbih invented it, so may Allah disgrace him for what he forged."
"299","Chapter: what one says after the adhan. Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba and Abd ibn Humayd said: Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated to us, from Musa ibn Ubayda, from Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Ata, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Ask Allah the Exalted for al-Wasila for me; no believer in this world asks it for me except that I shall be a witness or an intercessor for him on the Day of Resurrection."
"300","And Ahmad ibn Mani' said: Abu Mu'awiya narrated to us: Musa ibn Ubayda narrated to us with this. Al-Walid ibn Abd al-Malik followed him, from Musa ibn A'yan; al-Tabarani brought it in al-Awsat."
"301","Chapter: whoever gives the adhan, he gives the iqama. Abd ibn Humayd said: Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated to us: Sa'id al-Sammak narrated to us, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: Bilal, may Allah be pleased with him, was once late with the adhan, so a man gave the adhan; then Bilal, may Allah be pleased with him, came and wanted to give the iqama, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: He who gave the adhan gives the iqama."
"302","Chapter: when the prayer is commenced no prayer but the obligatory. Musaddad said: Yahya narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Sharik ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Namir, from Abu Salama, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saw a man praying the two rak'as while the prayer had been commenced, and said: Two prayers together? It is sound except that it is mursal."
"303","Chapter: the prayer times. Al-Harith said: al-Sakan ibn Nafi' narrated to us: Imran ibn Hudayr narrated to us, from Abu Mijlaz, who said: A man came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and asked him about the prayers; so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed Fajr in darkness, then prayed Asr in daylight; next day he waited for Fajr until it was said: what is keeping him? then he prayed, then he waited for Asr until it was said: what is keeping him? then he prayed, then he, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Where is the questioner? He said: here I am; he, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Did you witness us yesterday? He said: yes; he, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: And did you witness us today? He said: yes; he said: Whichever of that you intended is a time, and what is between them is a time."
"304","And Abu Ya'la said: Sa'id ibn Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Umawi narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from Kathir ibn Kathir, from Ali ibn Abd Allah, from Zayd ibn Haritha, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: A man asked the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about the time of the Fajr prayer, so he, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Pray it with me today and tomorrow. When he was at the valley of Namira at al-Juhfa he prayed it when dawn rose, then when we were at Dhu Tuwa he delayed it until people said: has the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, been taken? They said: if only we had prayed it. So he came out and prayed it just before the sun, then turned to the people and said: What did you say? They said: we said if only we had prayed. He, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Had you done so punishment would have befallen you. Then he called the questioner and said, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: The prayer is between these two times."
"305","And Ishaq said: Uthman ibn Umar informed us: Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us, from Muslim ibn Jundub, from al-Harith ibn Amr al-Hudhali, who said: Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, wrote to Abu Musa al-Ash'ari, may Allah be pleased with him: I have written concerning the prayer, and the most deserving thing Muslims observe is the matter of their religion; I saw the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, pray, I remembered of that what I remembered and forgot of it what I forgot; so pray Zuhr in the midday heat, Asr while the sun is alive, Maghrib at the fasting one's breaking, Isha so long as you do not fear people's sleep, and Fajr in darkness, and lengthen the recitation in it."
"306","And Ishaq said: Bishr ibn Umar al-Zahrani informed me: Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to us: Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us: Abu Bakr ibn Umar ibn Hazm narrated to me, from Abu Mas'ud al-Ansari, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: Jibril, peace be upon him, came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: stand and pray, and that was at the sun's decline when it tilted; so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, stood and prayed Zuhr four rak'as; the hadith in full."
"307","Isma'il ibn Abi Uways followed him, from Sulayman, with al-Bayhaqi, and he drove it in full. I say: its origin is in the two Sahihs from the hadith of Bashir ibn Abi Mas'ud without stating the times, and Abu Dawud brought it from his hadith with the statement of the times; and this chain is a good witness for Abu Dawud, and I brought it for the benefit. And al-Harith said: Dawud ibn al-Muhabbar narrated to us: Hammad, meaning Ibn Salama, narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Abu Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hazm, who said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him... and he mentioned it at length."
"308","And al-Harith ibn Abi Usama said: Yazid, that is Ibn Harun, narrated to us: Abd Allah ibn Awn narrated to us, from Muhammad, that is Ibn Sirin, from Abu Muhajir, who said: Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, wrote to Abu Musa al-Ash'ari, may Allah be pleased with him: pray Zuhr when the sun declines, Asr while the sun is alive, bright, pure, pray Maghrib when the sun disappears, or when the sun sets, and pray Isha when the twilight disappears until the first half of the night, for that is the sunna, and perform Fajr in darkness, and lengthen the recitation."
"309","And Ishaq said: Abd al-Razzaq informed us: Ma'mar narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Abi Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hazm, from his father, from his grandfather Amr ibn Hazm, who said: Jibril, peace be upon him, came and prayed with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed with the people when the sun declined; then he prayed Asr when his shadow was like him, then prayed Maghrib when the sun set, then prayed Isha after that as though intending the passing of the twilight, then prayed Fajr in darkness when dawn broke; then Jibril, peace be upon him, came next day and prayed Zuhr with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed Zuhr with the people when his shadow was like him, then prayed Asr when his shadow became twice him, then prayed Maghrib when the sun set at one time, then prayed Isha after a portion of the night had gone, then prayed Fajr making it bright. This chain is hasan, except that Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hazm did not hear from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, due to his young age; so if the pronoun in his grandfather refers to Abu Bakr, it depends on Abu Bakr's hearing from Amr."
"310","And Abu Ya'la said: Ghassan, that is Ibn al-Rabi', narrated to us, from Musa ibn Mutayr, from his father, who said: I asked Anas ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him: tell me of the prayer of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, which he regularly kept, for it has reached me that he delayed and advanced, but the prayer he regularly kept as though I am looking at it? He said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to pray Zuhr when the sun declined, and in summer he would cool it; he would pray Asr while the sun was white and pure; he would pray Maghrib when the sun's disk disappeared, departing while the stars' light was hardly seen; he would delay the last Isha until when he feared sleep he would say: O Bilal, call the adhan; and I heard him, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Were it not that my community would sleep through it, I would love to place it in a third of the night or half the night; and we would leave Fajr while seeing the stars' light. Part of it is in the Sunan by another way."
"311","And Ishaq said: Baqiyya ibn al-Walid informed us: Ishaq ibn Tha'laba narrated to me, from al-Hasan, from Ibn Mas'ud, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say regarding prayer: Do not bring it forward for leisure, nor delay it for need. This chain is weak."
"312","And Ibn Abi Umar said: Abd al-Majid ibn Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Rawwad narrated to us: Balhat ibn Abbad narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: We complained to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about the hot ground and he did not relieve us, and said: Seek help with there is no power nor strength except with Allah, for it repels ninety-nine doors of harm, the least of them anxiety."
"313","And Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba said: al-Fadl ibn Dukayn narrated to us: Isma'il ibn Ibrahim al-Madani narrated to us: Hurayr ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Rafi' ibn Khadij narrated to us, who said: I heard my grandfather Rafi' ibn Khadij, may Allah be pleased with him, say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: O Bilal, make Fajr bright to the extent that people see the places of their arrows."
"314","And Ibn Abi Umar said: al-Darawardi narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Asim ibn Umar ibn Qatada, from a man among the Companions, may Allah be pleased with them, who said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Pray Fajr in brightness, for whenever you pray it in brightness the reward is greater."
"315","And al-Bazzar narrated it and said: Sulayman ibn Ubayd Allah narrated to us: Abu Amir narrated to us: Fulayh narrated to us, from Asim ibn Umar, from his father, from his grandfather, and mentioned the like. And he said: We do not know anyone who followed Fulayh."
"316","And Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba said: Bakr ibn Abd Allah narrated to us: Isa ibn al-Mukhtar narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Isma'il ibn Umayya, from al-Zuhri, from Abd Allah ibn Ka'b, from Ka'b ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to pray Maghrib then people would return to their families while looking at the places of arrows when they shoot them."
"317","And Abu Bakr also said: Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from al-Ajlah, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, left Mecca at sunset and did not pray until he came to Sarif, which is nine miles from Mecca. In it is proof of the extension of Maghrib's time."
"318","And Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi said: Abd Allah ibn Hassan al-Abdi narrated to us: my two grandmothers Duhayba and Safiyya, daughters of Ulayba, narrated to me, from their stepdaughter and their father's grandmother Qayla bint Makhrama, that she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, led us in Fajr when dawn had split while the stars were intertwined in the sky, we could hardly recognize one another, and the men could hardly be recognized."
"319","And Musaddad said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Layth, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: No prayer is missed until the time of the next enters."
"320","Sufyan narrated to us, from Amr, that is Ibn Dinar, who said: We used to pray Fajr with Ibn al-Zubayr, may Allah be pleased with them both, then come to Jiyad and relieve ourselves then return. And Ibn al-Zubayr, may Allah be pleased with them both, said: We used to pray with Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, in darkness, and one of us would leave without recognizing his companion."
"321","And al-Harith said: Dawud ibn al-Muhabbar narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from his father, who said: al-Mughira ibn Shu'ba, may Allah be pleased with him, said to the Ansari who reminded him of the Asr time: Yes, bear witness that we used to pray Asr with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while the sun was white and pure, then come to Banu Amr ibn Awf, which is two miles from Medina, while the sun had not yet disappeared."
"322","And Abu Ya'la said: Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us: Abu Mu'awiya narrated to us: Ibn Abi Layla narrated to us, from Hafsa bint Azib, from al-Bara, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: A man came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, asking him about the prayer times, so he advanced and delayed and said: The time is between them."
"323","And Abu Ya'la said: Ibrahim ibn Sa'id al-Jawhari narrated to us: Asram ibn Hawshab narrated to us, from Ziyad ibn Sa'd, from al-Zuhri, from Salim ibn Abd Allah, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When the shade is a cubit and a half to two cubits, pray Zuhr. And the hadith of Abu Mahdhura, may Allah be pleased with him, preceded in the adhan chapter."
"324","And al-Harith said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Aban narrated to us: Amr al-Ju'fi narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Abd al-A'la, from Suwayd ibn Ghafala, from Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to make Fajr bright."
"325","And Abu Ya'la said: Mujahid ibn Musa narrated to us: Shababa narrated to us: Ayyub ibn Sinan narrated to me, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir, from Abu Bakr, from Bilal, may Allah be pleased with them, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who said: Pray Fajr in brightness, for it is greater in reward."
"326","And Ahmad ibn Mani' said: Ya'qub ibn al-Walid al-Madani narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Dhi'b, from al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayra, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: One of you prays a prayer, and what he missed of its time is harder upon him than his family and wealth."
"327","And Abu Ya'la said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Salih narrated to us: Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, that he heard a man called Ya'la say: Talq, may Allah be pleased with him, informed me that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: A man prays a prayer, and what he missed of its time is better than his family and wealth."
"328","Abu al-Rabi' narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us, from Asim, from Mus'ab ibn Sa'd, who said: I said to my father: O father, do you see His Exalted saying: Those who are heedless of their prayer, which of us does not forget? Which of us does not speak to himself? He said: That is not it; it is only wasting the time, idling until the time is lost."
"329","Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Wasiti narrated to us: Salih ibn Umar narrated to us: Hatim narrated to us, from Simak, from Mus'ab ibn Sa'd, who said: I asked my father: O father, Those who are heedless of their prayer, is one's forgetfulness in his prayer the talk of himself? Sa'd said: Do not all of us do that? But the heedless, and he mentioned it."
"330","Shayban ibn Farrukh narrated to us: Ikrima ibn Ibrahim al-Azdi narrated to us: Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr narrated to us, from Mus'ab ibn Sa'd, from his father, that he asked the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about Those who are heedless of their prayer, and he said: They are those who take the prayer out of its time. Al-Bazzar said: The memorizers narrated it stopped, and none raised it but Ikrima ibn Ibrahim."
"331","And Abu Ya'la said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us: Abd Allah ibn Nafi' narrated to us, from Umar ibn Dhakwan, from Dawud ibn Bukayr, from Ziyad ibn Abi Ziyad, from Anas ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: There will be after me wicked rulers who pray the prayer outside its time; when they do that, pray the prayer at its time and make your prayer with them supererogatory."
"332","Chapter: observing the times by the usual measures. Musaddad said: Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us: al-Ahwas ibn Hakim narrated to us, from Ubayda al-Yazani, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to like the white rooster, commanded taking it, and would say: It calls to prayer, wakes the sleeper, and drives away the jinn with its crowing."
"333","Musaddad said: Bishr narrated to me, from Zaynab, who said: A'isha, may Allah be pleased with her, used to take a rooster for the time of her prayer and the time of her suhur."
"334","Chapter: permissibility of combining Zuhr and Asr for a need. Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi said: Abu Bakr al-Hannat narrated to us: Yahya ibn Hani ibn Urwa narrated to me, from Abu Hudhayfa, from Abd al-Malik ibn Alqama al-Thaqafi, who said: The delegation of Thaqif came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and gave him a gift, and kept asking him and kept asking until they prayed Zuhr only with Asr."
"335","Chapter: delaying Asr and hastening it. Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba said: Muhammad ibn Abi Isma'il narrated to us, from Umara ibn Asim, who said: I entered upon Anas ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, and he mentioned the hadith; he said: Then the slave girl came to him and said: The prayer, may Allah keep you well! He said: Which prayer? She said: Asr prayer. He said: Have you prayed it? She said: I prayed it before entering to you. He said: Go back from me, Asr has not yet come. Then she returned to him and he said to her like his first saying, then she returned to him and said to him, so he said: I have heard what you said, hand me ablution water, for people pray this prayer before its time. Then he prayed."
"336","And Ibn Abi Umar said: Waki' narrated to us: Ziyad ibn Lahiq narrated to us, from a woman called Tamima, who said: I entered upon A'isha, may Allah be pleased with her, and she prayed Asr at the hour you call between the two prayers, then she, may Allah be pleased with her, said: We, the household of Muhammad, do not pray al-Sufayra."
"337","Chapter: cooling Zuhr. Musaddad said: Abd Allah ibn Dawud narrated to us: Hisham ibn Urwa narrated to us, from his father, I think from A'isha, may Allah be pleased with her, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Cool Zuhr in the heat."
"338","And Abu Ya'la said: Abd al-A'la ibn Hammad narrated to us: Abd Allah ibn Dawud narrated to us with it. Abu Ya'la said: Thus he narrated it to us with doubt."
"339","And al-Bazzar narrated it, saying: al-Qasim ibn Muhammad narrated to us: Abd Allah ibn Dawud narrated to us with its chain without doubt, with the wording: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The intensity of heat is from the breath of Hell, so cool the prayer. And he said: Strange, we know it from A'isha, may Allah be pleased with her, only by this way."
"340","Chapter: delaying Isha. Abu Ya'la said: Abu Khaythama narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Khazim narrated to us: Dawud ibn Abi Hind narrated to us, from Abu Nadra, from Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came out to his Companions one night while they were waiting for Isha, and said: People prayed and slept while you wait for it? Yet you are in prayer so long as you wait for it. Then he, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Were it not for the weakness of the weak and the age of the old, I would have delayed this prayer to half the night. Ibn Hibban brought it in his Sahih from Abu Ya'la. And Sa'dan ibn Nasr followed him, from Abu Mu'awiya Muhammad ibn Khazim."
"341","Chapter: dislike of calling it al-Atama. Musaddad said: Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Rawwad: a man of the people of Ta'if narrated to me, from Ghaylan ibn Shurahbil, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who said: Let not the Bedouins overcome you for the name of your prayer, for it is in the Book of Allah, mighty and majestic: Isha; Allah the Exalted said: And after the Isha prayer, three times of privacy for you. The Bedouins only call it al-Atama because of their camels and their milking."
"342","And Abu Ya'la said: Abu Khaythama narrated to us: Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us: Abd al-Aziz narrated to us with it."
"343","Chapter: dislike of sleeping before it. Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba said: Ibn Idris narrated to us, from Layth, from a man, from Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade sleep before it and conversation after it, meaning Isha."
"344","And Musaddad said: Ibrahim ibn Uqba narrated to me, saying: I heard Kabsha bint Ka'b say: I used to sleep before al-Atama, and when I heard the iqama I would stand and pray; it reached me that it is disliked, so I asked Anas ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, and he disliked it and said: Do not sleep before it."
"345","Chapter: conversation after Isha. Ibn Abi Umar said: Yahya ibn Sulaym narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwa, who said: I heard my father say: A'isha, Mother of the Believers, may Allah be pleased with her, heard my speech after the Isha which the Bedouins call al-Atama; he said: We were in a room between it and her palm leaves, and she said: O Urayya, or O Urwa, what is this night talk? I never saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sleeping before this prayer, nor talking after it: either sleeping and safe, or praying and gaining."
"346","And Abu Ya'la said: Harun ibn Ma'ruf narrated to us: Ibn Wahb narrated to us: Mu'awiya ibn Salih narrated to us: Abu Hamza narrated to me, from A'isha wife of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, may Allah be pleased with her, who said: I never saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sleeping before Isha, nor idling after it: either remembering and gaining, or sleeping and safe."
"347","Mu'awiya said: And Abu Abd Allah al-Ansari narrated to me, from A'isha wife of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, may Allah be pleased with her, who said: Night talk is for three: for a bridegroom, or a traveler, or one keeping vigil at night."
"348","And Abu Bakr said: Ubayd Allah narrated to us: Umar ibn Wasil informed us, from his father, from A'isha, may Allah be pleased with her, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever sleeps before Isha, may he not sleep."
"349","Chapter: supplication in prayer. Abu Ya'la said: Ahmad ibn Isa al-Tustari narrated to us: Ibn Wahb narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Abi Ayyub, from Khalid ibn Yazid, from Abu Rafi', may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Ask Allah the Exalted for your needs in the Fajr prayer. Its men are trustworthy, except that it is broken if Abu Rafi' is the Companion; otherwise it is mursal or mu'dal."
"350","Chapter: the times prayer is forbidden in. Ishaq said: Amr ibn Muhammad al-Qurashi informed us: al-Layth ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from al-Maqburi, from Awn ibn Abd Allah ibn Utba, from Ibn Mas'ud, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: While we were with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, Amr ibn Abasa, may Allah be pleased with him, came to him, and he had pledged the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, upon Islam, and said: Tell me, O Muhammad, of what you know and I am ignorant of, and asked him about the hours of prayer; so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to him: When you have prayed Maghrib, prayer is accepted and witnessed until you pray Fajr; then avoid prayer until the sun rises and turns white, for the sun rises between the two horns of Satan; when it turns white and rises, prayer is accepted and witnessed until midday and the sun stands level and everything stands in its shade, and it is the hour Hell is stoked; when the sun declines, prayer is accepted and witnessed until the sun turns yellow, for the sun sets between the two horns of Satan."
"351","Al-Layth said: And one of our brothers narrated to me, from al-Maqburi in this hadith, that he said: Except on Friday, for there is no harm in prayer at midday then, because Hell is not stoked in it. I say: This text Ahmad and others narrated by way of Amr ibn Abasa himself, and this way is a witness for it; and this chain is sound, except that in it is a break, because Awn did not meet Abd Allah ibn Mas'ud, may Allah be pleased with him, and there have come from him hadiths of his narration from his father, from Ibn Mas'ud, may Allah be pleased with him, other than this."
"352","And Ishaq said: Jarir informed us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Ata, who said: We left for the funeral of Rafi' ibn Khadij, may Allah be pleased with him, after Fajr prayer, and al-Walid ibn Utba was over the people; he wanted to pray over it, so Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, stood and shouted at the top of his voice: Do not pray over your dead until the sun rises. So the commander and the people sat. This chain is hasan, stopped, and Malik has in al-Muwatta by another way from Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, the like."
"353","And Ishaq said: Abu Amir al-Aqadi informed us: Zuhayr, that is Ibn Muhammad, narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Khusayfa, from Salama ibn al-Akwa', may Allah be pleased with him, who said: I used to travel with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and never saw him pray after Asr nor after Fajr."
"354","And Abu Bakr said: Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr narrated to us: Zuhayr narrated to us with it. This chain is hasan."
"355","And Musaddad said: Harb ibn Abi al-Aliya narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, who said: A man saw Abu al-Darda, may Allah be pleased with him, pray when the sun had turned yellow, and said: O companions of Muhammad, do you forbid prayer after Fajr and after Asr?! He said: Yes, except that this House is not like others."
"356","And Musaddad said: Yahya narrated to us: Anbasa al-Wazzan narrated to us, who said: We were at a funeral in which was Budayl, and he said, while the sun was yellow upon the edges of the walls: Do not pray at this hour. So Abu Umama, may Allah be pleased with him, said: I prayed with Abu Hurayra, may Allah be pleased with him, over a funeral at this hour."
"357","Abu Bakr said: Abu Mu'awiya narrated to us, from al-Ifriqi Abd al-Rahman ibn Ziyad ibn An'um, from Abd Allah ibn Yazid, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: No prayer after Fajr except two rak'as."
"358","And Ibn Abi Umar said: al-Muqri narrated to us: Abd al-Rahman ibn Ziyad narrated to us with it."
"359","And Abd ibn Humayd said: Ya'la narrated to us: al-Ifriqi narrated to us with it."
"360","And Ibn Abi Umar said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Hujayr, from Tawus, that he used to pray after Asr, so Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, forbade him. So Tawus said: It was only forbidden to take it as a ladder. Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, said: It is not for a believing man nor a believing woman, when Allah and His Messenger have decreed a matter, to have choice in their matter, the verse; and I do not know whether you will be punished for it or rewarded. Its chain is sound, and its origin is in al-Nasa'i."
"361","And Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba said: Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated to us, from Shu'ba, from Simak ibn Harb, who said: I heard al-Muhallab ibn Abi Sufra narrate from Samura ibn Jundub, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade praying after Fajr until the sun rises, for it rises upon the horn, or the two horns, of Satan."
"362","And Musaddad said: Abu Awana narrated to us, from Mughira, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, who said: Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, used to strike for the two rak'as after Asr. Its chain is sound, and it is in the Sahih by another way."
"363","And Abu Dawud said: Shu'ba narrated to us: Abu al-Tayyah informed me, from Ma'bad al-Juhani, who said: Mu'awiya, may Allah be pleased with him, addressed us and said: Why do people pray a prayer when I accompanied the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and never saw him pray it, and we heard him forbid it, meaning the two rak'as after Asr."
"364","And al-Harith said: Sa'id ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Bayan, from Wabara, who said: Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, saw Tamim al-Dari, may Allah be pleased with him, praying after Asr and struck him with the stick; Tamim said: Why, O Umar, do you strike me for a prayer I prayed with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him? So Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, said: O Tamim, not all people know what you know."
"365","And al-Harith said: Muhammad ibn Umar narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Muslim, that he heard al-Maqburi narrate from Abu Hurayra, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade prayer at midday except on Friday."
"366","And Abu Ya'la said: Hudba and Ibrahim al-Sami narrated to us, both saying: Aban narrated to us, from Yahya, that Qurra ibn Abi Qurra narrated to him that Abu Usayd narrated to him that he saw a man praying after Asr, so he rebuked him and said: Do not pray after Asr, for I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: No prayer after Asr; the wording of Hudba."
"367","Al-Harith: Asim ibn Ali narrated to us: Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abd al-Qari, who said: I circumambulated with Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, after Fajr prayer, then he rode and did not reach morning brightness until he came to Dhu Tuwa, and prayed two rak'as."
"368","And Abu Ya'la said: Harun ibn Ma'ruf narrated to us: Abd Allah ibn Wahb narrated to us: Makhrama informed us, from his father, from Sa'id ibn Nafi', who said: Abu Hubayra al-Ansari, a companion of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saw me while I was praying Fajr when the sun had risen, so he faulted me for that and forbade me, then said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Do not pray until the sun rises, for it only rises in the horn of Satan."
"369","And he said: Ibn Numayr narrated to us: Rawh narrated to us: Usama ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Hafs ibn Ubayd Allah, from Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Do not pray at sunrise nor at sunset, for it rises and sets upon the horn of Satan, and pray between that as you wish."
"370","Chapter: no obligatory prayer besides the five. Abu Dawud said: Zam'a narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Idris, who said: I was sitting in a gathering in which was Ubada, may Allah be pleased with him, and he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Jibril, peace be upon him, came to me from Allah the Exalted and said: O Muhammad, Allah the Exalted says: I have obligated upon your community five prayers; whoever fulfills them with their ablution, their times, their bowing and their prostration, then he has with Me a covenant for them that I shall admit him by them to Paradise; the hadith."
"371","And Abd ibn Humayd said: Abd al-Razzaq informed us: Ma'mar informed us, from Abu Harun al-Abdi, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: Prayer was obligated upon the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, on the night of al-Isra fifty prayers, then it was reduced until made five; then Allah, mighty and majestic, said: You have in the five fifty; the good deed is tenfold."
"372","And Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba said: Hubayb ibn Habib, brother of Hamza al-Zayyat, narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Ayzar ibn Hurayth, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: A Bedouin came to him and said: O Ibn Abbas, we are Muslims, and here are some Emigrants claiming we are upon nothing. So Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, said: The Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever establishes prayer, gives zakat, performs Hajj to the House, fasts Ramadan, and honors the guest enters Paradise."
"373","Chapter: facing the qibla and the sutra for the praying one. Abu Ya'la said: Yahya ibn Abd al-Hamid al-Himmani narrated to us: Qays ibn al-Rabi' narrated to us, from Ziyad ibn Ilaqa, from Umara ibn Aws, may Allah be pleased with him, and he had prayed toward both qiblas, who said: I was in my house when a caller called at the door: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, has turned to the Ka'ba. So I bear witness over our imam and the men, women and children that they prayed to here, meaning Bayt al-Maqdis, and to here, meaning the Ka'ba."
"374","And he also said: Mus'ab, that is Ibn Abd Allah al-Zubayri, narrated to us: Bishr ibn al-Sari narrated to me, from Mus'ab ibn Thabit, from Hisham, from his father, from A'isha, may Allah be pleased with her, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Press close to the qibla."
"375","Harun ibn Ma'ruf narrated to us: Bishr ibn al-Sari narrated to us with it."
"376","And Abu Ya'la said: Muhammad ibn Bakkar narrated to us: Hassan ibn Ibrahim narrated to us: Sa'id ibn Masruq narrated to us, from Husayn ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Shaybani, from Mu'awiya ibn Qurra, from Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: I do not recognize anything of people's affairs except the qibla."
"377","Abu al-Rabi' narrated to us: Abu Shihab al-Hannat narrated to us, from Hamza al-Nasibi, from Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The noblest of sittings are those faced toward the qibla."
"378","And Ahmad ibn Mani' said: Hushaym narrated to us: Ya'la ibn Ata narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Qamta, who said: I saw Abd Allah ibn Amr, may Allah be pleased with them both, in the Sacred Mosque beside the spout, saying: Allah, mighty and majestic, said to His Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: We shall turn you to a qibla you approve; so this is the qibla, this is the qibla."
"379","And al-Harith said: al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Azraq narrated to us: Abd al-Warith narrated to us: Ishaq ibn Suwayd narrated to us, who said: Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, saw a man praying far from the qibla and said: Come forward, do not spoil your prayer; and I said to you only what I heard from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying it."
"380","And Abu Ya'la said: al-Jarrah ibn Makhlad al-Basri narrated to us: Husam ibn Abbad ibn Yazid al-Qurashi narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn Abi Mahdhura narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, enter the mosque from the side of the Banu Shayba gate, until he came facing the Ka'ba; he faced the qibla and drew a line before him crosswise, then said takbir and prayed, while people circumambulated between the line and the Ka'ba."
"381","Al-Harith: Dawud ibn al-Muhabbar narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us, from Abu Harun al-Abdi, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: A woman and a dog cut off prayer. I said: What screens me? He, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: An arrow, a saddle, and a stone."
"382","And Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba said: Abu Khalid al-Ahmar narrated to us, from Hajjaj, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Muhallab ibn Abi Sufra, from a man among the Companions of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: If between you and one passing before you is like the back of a saddle, it has screened you."
"383","And Ahmad ibn Mani' said: Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri narrated to us, from Hajjaj, the like, and said: One who heard the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, informed me."
"384","Chapter: striving for the qibla. Al-Harith said: Dawud ibn Amr narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Yazid al-Wasiti narrated to us, from Muhammad, that is Ibn Salim, from Ata, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: We were with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, on a journey or expedition, and cloud befell us; so we exerted our judgment and differed about the qibla; each of us prayed drawing a line before him that we may know our places; in the morning we looked and found we had prayed to other than the qibla; we mentioned that to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he did not command us to repeat, and said: Your prayer has sufficed. Muhammad ibn Ubayd Allah al-Arzami followed him from Ata. And it was also narrated from Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Sulayman from Ata."
"385","Chapter: covering the private parts. Ishaq said: Rawh ibn Ubada informed us: Abbad ibn Mansur informed us: Ikrima ibn Khalid narrated to me, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Asim ibn Damra, from Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, that he used to enter upon the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him; one day he entered upon him while he had uncovered his thighs, and he said: O son of Abu Talib, do not uncover your thigh, for it is private, and do not look at the thigh of the living nor the dead, for you wash the dead. I say: Ahmad, Abu Dawud and Ibn Maja brought it from the hadith of Ibn Jurayj from Habib with its chain, without his saying: for it is private, and without his saying: for you wash the dead."
"386","And al-Haytham ibn Kulayb al-Shashi narrated it: Muhammad ibn Sa'd al-Awfi narrated to us: Rawh ibn Ubada narrated to us: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us: Habib ibn Abi Thabit narrated to me, from Asim ibn Damra, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, entered upon me while I was uncovering my thigh, and said: O Ali, cover your thigh, for it is part of the private parts."
"387","And Musaddad said: Isma'il narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us: Abu al-Rijal Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman informed us, from his mother Amra, may Allah be pleased with her, who said: A'isha, may Allah be pleased with her, said: A woman does not pray in less than three garments for one who is able."
"388","Hushaym narrated to us, from Mujalid, who said: Masruq was asked: How does a slave woman pray? He said: As she goes out."
"389","And Ahmad ibn Mani' said: Ibn Ulayya narrated to us: Sulayman al-Taymi narrated to us, from Ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayra, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, said: A woman prays in three garments. This chain is sound."
"390","And Abu Bakr said: Muhammad ibn Umar al-Aslami narrated to us: al-Dahhak ibn Uthman narrated to us, from Habib, freedman of Urwa, who said: I heard Asma bint Abi Bakr, may Allah be pleased with them both, say: I saw my father pray in a single garment, with his clothes laid aside, and he said: O daughter, the last prayer the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed, he prayed in a single garment."
"391","And Abu Ya'la said: Abu Bakr narrated to us with it."
"392","And al-Harith said: Abu al-Nadr narrated to us: al-Layth narrated to us, from Bukayr ibn Abd Allah, from Busr ibn Sa'id, from Ubayd Allah al-Khawlani, foster son of Maymuna, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: I saw Maymuna wife of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, pray in a flowing tight tunic and a headcover, with no waist-wrapper upon her. Sound, stopped."
"393","And Abu Ya'la said: Abdan narrated to us: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj ibn Artat, who said: I asked Ata about people who drown and come out naked, how do they pray? He said: If they find grass they cover with it, otherwise they pray sitting, their imam among them, or he said in their midst."
"394","And Abu Dawud said: Adi ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, from Abu Hazim, from Sahl ibn Sa'd, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: Most of those who prayed behind the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, were the people of knots. I said: Who are the people of knots? He said: None of them had but one garment which he would knot upon his neck."
"395","Chapter: permissibility of prayer in a single garment. Ishaq said: More than one informed me, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi, from Ya'la ibn al-Harith, from Ghaylan ibn Jami' al-Muharibi, from Iyas ibn Salama ibn al-Akwa', from a son of Ammar ibn Yasir, from his father: I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, pray in a single garment wrapped around him."
"396","And Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba said: Ahmad ibn Abd Allah ibn Yunus narrated to us: Ya'la ibn al-Harith al-Muharibi narrated to us, saying: I heard Ghaylan ibn Jami' say: Iyas ibn Salama narrated to us, from a son of Ammar ibn Yasir, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: My father, may Allah be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, led us in a single garment wrapped around him."
"397","And Abu Ya'la said: Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us: Ya'la ibn al-Harith narrated to us with it."
"398","He said: And Musa ibn Muhammad narrated to us: Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us with it."
"399","And Abu Bakr said: Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Ata al-Khurasani, from Mu'awiya ibn Abi Sufyan, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: I visited my sister Umm Habiba, may Allah be pleased with her, and saw the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, pray in a single garment with its two ends crossed."
"400","And Abu Ya'la said: Ishaq ibn Yahya narrated to us: Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated to us with it."
"401","Ibrahim ibn al-Husayn narrated to us: Mubashshir, meaning Ibn Isma'il, and al-Harith ibn Atiyya, and Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated to us, from al-Awza'i, from Ya'ish ibn al-Walid, from Mu'awiya, may Allah be pleased with him, the like."
"402","And Musaddad said: Mu'tamir narrated to us, from Burd ibn Sinan, from Ubada ibn Nusayy, from Ghudayf ibn al-Harith, who said: I came to Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, and said: We go out every year, and I have a small structure; if I pray in it the woman is beside me, and if I go out I am exposed. He said: Cut between you both with a garment, then pray as you wish."
"403","And Musaddad said: Hammad narrated to us, from Abu Harun, who said: I heard Abu Sa'id, may Allah be pleased with him, say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: It does not harm one of you to pray in his garment wrapped, but let him knot it so it does not distract him from his prayer."
"404","And Musaddad said: Yahya narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Uthman ibn al-Mughira, from Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd, from Muhammad ibn al-Hanafiyya, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, saw no harm in a man praying in a single garment, and he used to pray in a single garment with its two ends crossed."
"405","And he said: Yahya narrated to us: Isma'il narrated to me, from Qays, who said: I saw Khalid ibn al-Walid, may Allah be pleased with him, leading people in the army in a single garment."
"406","And al-Harith said: Dawud ibn al-Muhabbar narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came out leaning upon Usama ibn Zayd, may Allah be pleased with them both, wearing a Qitri garment, with no other garment upon him."
"407","And Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba said: Isma'il narrated to us, from al-Jurayri, from Abu Nadra, who said: Ubayy, may Allah be pleased with him, said: Prayer in a single garment is good; we did it with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"408","Chapter: what one prays upon and in. Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba said: Yazid ibn al-Miqdam ibn Shurayh ibn Hani narrated to us, from his father, from Shurayh, that he asked A'isha, may Allah be pleased with her: Did the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, pray upon a mat, for I heard in the Book of Allah, mighty and majestic: And We made Hell a mat for the disbelievers? She, may Allah be pleased with her, said: No, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, did not pray upon it."
"409","And Abu Ya'la said: Abu Bakr narrated to us with this."
"410","And Abu Ya'la said: Abu al-Rabi' narrated to us: Sallam ibn Sulaym narrated to us, from Zayd al-Ammi, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prostrate upon his garment."
"411","And Musaddad said: Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Thabit ibn Ubayd, who said: I entered upon Zayd ibn Thabit, may Allah be pleased with him, and saw him pray upon a mat, and prostrate upon it."
"412","Muhammad ibn Jabir narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, who said: I saw al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, may Allah be pleased with them both, pray upon a board."
"413","And Musaddad said: Yahya narrated to us, from Abd al-Hamid ibn Ja'far, from his father, from some of Umar's children, from Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: I do not like to pray in this closed house of theirs, meaning the enclosure."
"414","Chapter: what one prays toward and what one does not pray toward. Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba and Ahmad ibn Mani', both saying: Hushaym narrated to us: Humayd informed us, from Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: I was praying toward a grave, and Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, saw me and kept saying: The grave, the grave; I kept not understanding what he meant, so I raised my head to the sky, and he said: The grave is before you."
"415","Both said: And Hushaym narrated to us: Mansur informed us, from al-Hasan, from Anas, from Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, the like. This report is sound; al-Bukhari attached it."
"416","And al-Harith said: Ya'la ibn Abbad narrated to us: Abd al-Hakam narrated to us, from Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: A dog, a donkey and a woman cut off prayer."
"417","And Musaddad said: Yahya narrated to us, from Shu'ba, from Sa'd ibn Ibrahim, from his father, who said: I was praying and a man passed before me and I stopped him; I asked Uthman ibn Affan, may Allah be pleased with him, and he said: O son of my brother, it does not harm you."
"418","Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Atiq and Ayyub, from Muhammad, who said: Abu Sa'id, may Allah be pleased with him, was praying and al-Harith passed before him, or wanted to pass before him, until he nearly took his hair; al-Harith complained to Marwan, so Abu Sa'id came to Marwan, and Marwan said: If you obey this one and his companions they will Judaize you. So Abu Sa'id, may Allah be pleased with him, said: By Allah you have lied; were you and your father to become Jews we would not become Jews with you both. Ayyub said: Muhammad said: He spoke the truth; Judaism was offered to them in the pre-Islamic age and they refused it."
"419","Chapter: forbidding striking those who pray. Abu Ya'la said: Sufyan ibn Waki' narrated to us: my father narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Abi Abd Allah, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Jud'an, from his grandmother, from Umm Salama, may Allah be pleased with her, who said: Abu al-Haytham ibn al-Tayyihan came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and sought a servant from him; the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, promised him if he got captives. Then he met Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: O Abu al-Haytham, the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, has got captives. He said: Go to him, for he will fulfill your promise. So Abu al-Haytham and Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, went to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, said to him: O Messenger of Allah, Abu al-Haytham has come to you to claim your promise? The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to him: We have got two black boys, choose whichever you wish. He said: I consult you. He, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Take this, for he prayed with us; and do not strike him, for we have been forbidden from striking those who pray. Al-Tirmidhi brought from it: The one consulted is trusted, in brief."
"420","And Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba said: Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, from Musa ibn Ubayda: Hud ibn Ata narrated to me, from Anas ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade striking those who pray."
"421","And Abu Ya'la said: Abu Bakr narrated to us, and mentioned it."
"422","And Amr ibn al-Dahhak ibn Makhlad narrated to us: my father narrated to us: Musa narrated to us with it. And Musa is weak."
"423","Chapter: when a boy is commanded to pray. Ahmad ibn Mani' said: al-Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us: Ibn Lahi'a narrated to us, from Amr ibn al-Harith, who said: Sa'id ibn Abi Hilal informed him, from a man among them, from his uncle, who said: We asked the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about children's prayer? He said: When one of them knows his right from his left, command him to pray."
"424","And al-Harith said: Dawud ibn al-Muhabbar narrated to us: Abd Allah ibn al-Muthanna ibn Abd Allah ibn Anas ibn Malik narrated to us, from his uncle Thumama ibn Abd Allah ibn Anas, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Command them to pray at seven, and strike them for it at thirteen. Dawud is abandoned, and he contradicted in this hadith in chain and text."
"425","Chapter: building mosques and widening them. Abu Dawud said: Muhammad ibn Dirham al-Azdi narrated to us: Ka'b ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Azdi narrated to me, from Ibn Abi Qatada al-Ansari, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came to us while we were building the mosque, and said: Widen it, you will fill it."
"426","And Abu Ya'la said: Musa ibn Muhammad ibn Hayyan narrated to us: Salm ibn Qutayba narrated to us: Abd Allah ibn Umar narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, said: Were it not that I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: I wish to extend our qibla side, I would not have extended."
"427","Abu Khaythama narrated to us: Abd Allah ibn Maslama ibn Qa'nab narrated to us: Abd Allah ibn Umar narrated to us the like. Al-Umari said: So he extended what is between the minbar and the place of the enclosure."
"428","And Musaddad said: Yahya narrated to us, from Shu'ba: Abu Ishaq narrated to us, from Amr ibn Maymun, from the Companions of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who said: Mosques are Allah's houses on earth."
"429","And Abu Ya'la said: Zuhayr ibn Harb narrated to us: Jarir narrated to us, from Ata, from Muharib ibn Dithar, from Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: A man came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, which lands are worst? He said: I do not know, or he was silent. Then he said to him: Which lands are best? He said: I do not know, or he was silent. Then Jibril, peace be upon him, came to him and he asked him, and he said: I do not know. He said: Ask your Lord. He said: We do not ask Him about anything. And he trembled a trembling that the soul of the Prophet Muhammad, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, almost ascended from it. When Jibril, peace be upon him, ascended, Allah, mighty and majestic, said: Muhammad asked you: which lands are best? And you said: I do not know? He said: Yes. He said: Then tell him that the best of lands are the mosques, and the worst of lands are the markets. Ibn Hibban declared it sound."
"430","Chapter: merit of one who builds a mosque. Ishaq said: Isa ibn Yunus informed us, from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, from his father, from Abu Dharr, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: Whoever builds for Allah a mosque, even like a sandgrouse's nest, Allah builds for him a house in Paradise."
"431","And Ishaq said: Jarir and Abu Mu'awiya informed us, meaning from al-A'mash, with this chain the like."
"432","And Ahmad ibn Mani' said: Hushaym narrated to us, from Mansur, from al-Hakam ibn Utayba, from Yazid ibn Sharik, from Abu Dharr, who said: Whoever builds for Allah a mosque like a sandgrouse's nest, a house is built for him in Paradise and a good deed is written for him."
"433","And Ishaq said: al-Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman informed us, from al-Hajjaj, from al-Hakam ibn Utayba, from Ibrahim al-Taymi, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever builds a mosque, and mentioned the like."
"434","And Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba said: Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us: Qutba narrated to us, from al-A'mash, with it, raised."
"435","Al-Ruyani narrated it in his Musnad: al-Abbas ibn Muhammad narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us: Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from al-A'mash, with it, raised. Ibn Yunus said: It was said to Abu Bakr: None raised it but you? He said: I heard it from al-A'mash when he was young."
"436","351/7 - Al-Bazzar said: Salm ibn Junadah narrated to us, Waki' narrated - in his house - from Sufyan al-Thawri, from al-A'mash, raised (to the Prophet). Al-Bazzar said: We do not know anyone who corroborated Salm ibn Junadah in this; it is only known from the hadith of Ahmad ibn Yunus, from Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash."
"437","351/8 - Abu Ya'la narrated it - in his Musnad -: Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Ar'arah narrated to us, Yahya ibn Adam narrated, from Qutbah ibn al-Ala, from al-A'mash, with it, raised. 351/9 - Muhammad ibn Harb al-Nasha'i narrated it, from Muhammad ibn Ubayd, from his brother Ya'la ibn Ubayd, from al-A'mash, with it, raised as well."
"438","I have gathered its paths of transmission in a large volume in which I wrote from more than thirty Companions. 245 - [Al-Harith] said: Dawud narrated to us, Maysarah narrated, from Abu A'ishah al-Sa'di, from Yazid ibn Umar, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurayrah and Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them), who both said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed us - then he mentioned a long hadith - and in it: 'Whoever builds a mosque for Allah, Allah gives him, for every handspan - or he said: for every cubit - forty thousand thousand cities of gold, silver, pearls, ruby and pearl; in every city forty thousand palaces; in every palace seventy thousand houses; in every house a thousand rooms; in every room forty thousand beds; upon every bed a wife from the wide-eyed houris; and in every house forty thousand maidservants; and in every house forty thousand tables; upon every table forty thousand bowls; in every bowl forty thousand kinds of food; and Allah Almighty gives His ally the strength to attend to those wives and that food and drink in a single day.' This is a fabricated hadith."
"439","352/1 - Abu Dawud [al-Tayalisi] said: Shu'bah narrated to us, Jabir informed me, from Ammar, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'Whoever builds a mosque, even like a sandgrouse's nesting hollow for its eggs, Allah builds for him a house in Paradise.'"
"440","352/2 - Al-Harith [ibn Abi Usamah] and Abu Ya'la, both together, said: Yahya ibn Abd al-Hamid al-Himmani narrated to us, Sharik narrated, from Ammar al-Duhni, and he mentioned it with the wording: 'Whoever builds a mosque for Allah, Allah builds for him a house in Paradise.'"
"441","353/1 - Musaddad said: Abdullah ibn Dawud narrated to us, Kathir ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Tahhan narrated, Ata narrated to me, from A'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'Whoever builds a mosque, Allah builds for him a house in Paradise.' She said: I said: O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and these mosques along the road to Makkah? He said: 'And those too.'"
"442","353/2 - Ibn Abi Umar said: Marwan narrated to us, from Kathir al-Mu'addib, with it. And in it: 'Even the measure of a sandgrouse's nesting hollow.'"
"443","354 - Abu Ya'la said: Bishr - that is Ibn al-Walid - narrated to us, Sulayman narrated, Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'Whoever builds a house in which Allah is worshipped from lawful earnings, Allah builds for him a house in Paradise of pearls and ruby.'"
"444","36 - Chapter on the dislike of building mosques for other than prayer in them. 355 - Musaddad said: Isma'il narrated to us, from Ayyub; a man narrated to me that Anas ibn Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) passed by before the sweeping plague, and he would pass by a newly built mosque and ask about it, and it would be said: This is a mosque newly built by the sons of so-and-so. So he said: It used to be said: 'There will come upon people a time when they build mosques and boast of them, then populate them only a little.' Ayyub said: Then the sweeping plague came and swept them away. Al-Bukhari cited it as a suspended narration, and it has been narrated raised (to the Prophet)."
"445","37 - Chapter on keeping mosques free (of impurities and distractions). 356 - [Ishaq] said: Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Muhammad ibn Muslim narrated, from Abd Rabbihi, from Makhul, from Mu'adh (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): 'Keep your mosques clear of your children and your insane, of carrying out your legal punishments, of drawing your swords, of your buying and selling, and of your disputes; perfume them with incense on the day of your Friday congregation, and place places of purification at their doors.' This is disconnected."
"446","357 - [Ishaq said]: Abu Mu'awiyah informed us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated, from Talhah ibn [Ubayd Allah] ibn Kurayz, from Abu Ayyub al-Ansari (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: A man took a louse from his garment [and threw it] in the mosque, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: 'Put it back in your garment.' This is disconnected."
"447","358 - [Ishaq said]: Yazid ibn Harun informed us, Muhammad narrated, from Talhah ibn Abd Allah ibn Kurayz, from an elder of the people of Madinah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a man who had taken a louse, then he mentioned the like of it."
"448","359 - [Ishaq said]: Yahya ibn Adam informed us, Ibn al-Mubarak reported, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from his father, from Jubayr ibn Mut'im (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): 'That legal punishments are not carried out in mosques, nor poetry recited in them, nor weapons drawn in them.' This is a good chain if Ishaq ibn [Yasar] heard it from Jubayr (may Allah be pleased with him)."
"449","360 - Al-Harith said: Muhammad ibn Umar narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Hazim narrated, from Abu al-Ash'ath, from Nafi' ibn Jubayr ibn Mut'im, from his father (may Allah be pleased with him), raised: 'Legal punishments are not carried out in mosques.'"
"450","361 - Musaddad said: Hammad narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abu Raja, who said: I heard Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) delivering a sermon on a rainy day, and he said: 'Pray in your dwellings, and do not carry this filth on your feet into the mosque, for not all the neighbours of the mosque can bear your purification (from the mud).'"
"451","362 - Abu Bakr said: Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, al-Husayn ibn Waqid narrated, from Abu Ghalib, from Abu Umamah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'Spitting in the mosque is an offence, and burying it is a good deed.'"
"452","363 - Musaddad said: Yahya narrated to us, from Shu'bah, from Abu Ishaq, from Harithah ibn Mudarrib, who said: Abdullah said: 'When you see an old man reciting poetry in the mosque on Friday and recalling the days of ignorance, strike his head with a stick.' Sahih, halted."
"453","364 - [Al-Humaydi] said: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in a dream, and I said [to him]: O Messenger of Allah, what do you think of this hadith narrated from you: 'The angels are offended by what the children of Adam are offended by'? He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'True.'"
"454","365 - He said: Sufyan narrated to us, Abu al-Zubayr narrated, who said: I heard Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him), asked about garlic, say: 'There was no garlic in our land that day; what was forbidden was only onions and leeks.'"
"455","366 - [Ahmad] ibn Mani' said: Abu Ahmad narrated to us, Isra'il narrated, from Muslim - that is al-A'war - from [Habbah], from Ali (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: 'The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us to eat garlic,' and said: 'Were it not that the angel descends upon me, I would eat it.' The hadith of Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) on the dislike of sleeping in the mosque will come in the virtues of Ali (may Allah be pleased with him)."
"456","38 - Chapter on the merit of keeping to the mosque. 367 - Abu Dawud said: Muhammad ibn Abi Humayd narrated to us, Sa'id al-Mahri narrated, from Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'The best guarding of the frontiers is waiting for prayer and keeping to gatherings of remembrance; there is no servant who prays then sits in his place of prayer but the angels keep invoking blessings upon him until he breaks his ablution or stands up.'"
"457","368/1 - Ibn Abi Shaybah said: Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Ata, from Abu Abd al-Rahman; one who heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) narrated to me, saying: 'Whoever sits in his place of prayer or enters a mosque for prayer, the angels keep invoking blessings upon him so long as he remains in his sitting place, so long as he does not break his ablution: O Allah, forgive him; O Allah, have mercy on him.'"
"458","368/2 - Al-Harith said: [Dawud ibn Rushayd] narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, who said: We visited Abdullah ibn Habib - that is Abu Abd al-Rahman - while he was passing away - i.e. dying - in his mosque, and I said: If only you would move to your bed? He said: One who heard (the Prophet) narrated to me, then he mentioned it. And he said at its end: So I wish to die while I am in my mosque."
"459","369 - Musaddad said: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, Yunus ibn Ubayd narrated, who said: I said to al-Hasan - or it was said to him -: What do you think of his saying: 'The servant remains in prayer so long as he remains in his place of prayer'? I said: His sitting place in which he prays? He said: 'Rather, the whole mosque.'"
"460","370 - Yahya narrated to us, from Ibn Ajlan, from Sa'id al-Maqburi, from Sa'id ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) - he did not raise it - who said: 'There is no man who frequents the mosques, then illness or ailment keeps him from them, then he returns, but Allah rejoices at him...' the hadith. Sahih, halted; Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated it from Sa'id [raised], shorter than it."
"461","371 - Al-Harith said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far al-Warkani narrated to us, Mu'tamir narrated, from Fayyad ibn Ghazwan, from Muhammad ibn Atiyyah, from Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) [raised]: 'Allah Almighty will surely call out on the Day of Resurrection: Where are My neighbours? So the angels will say: Our Lord, who deserves to be Your neighbour? Then He will say: Where are those who frequented the mosques?'"
"462","372/1 - Abu Dawud said: Salih al-Murri narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'Those who frequent the mosques of Allah Almighty [are] the people of Allah.'"
"463","372/2 - Abd ibn Humayd said: Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Salih narrated, with it."
"464","372/3 - Abu Ya'la said: Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj al-Nili narrated to us."
"465","372/4 - Al-Bazzar said: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ghiyath narrated to us. Both said: Salih narrated, with it. And al-Bazzar said: We do not know anyone who narrated it from Thabit except Salih. And al-Tabarani said the same in al-Awsat."
"466","373 - Ibn Abi Umar said: Marwan al-Fazari narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid, from a man, from Muhammad ibn Wasi', who said: Abu al-Darda (may Allah be pleased with him) said to his son: O my son, let your house be the mosque, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: 'The mosque is the house of the God-fearing; whoever's houses are the mosques, Allah completes for him relief, mercy, and passage over the Bridge to Paradise.'"
"467","374/1 - Al-Muqri narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Ziyad narrated, from Abdullah - that is Ibn Yazid al-Hubuli - from Abdullah ibn Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'There are six gatherings: no Muslim is in any of them but he is guaranteed by Allah Almighty: in the path of Allah Almighty, or in a congregational mosque, or visiting a sick person, or following a funeral, or in his house, or with a just ruler whom he honours and respects.'"
"468","374/2 - Abd [ibn Humayd] said: Abdullah ibn Yazid al-Muqri narrated to us, with it."
"469","374/3 - Al-Bazzar said: Muslim narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Yazid narrated, with it."
"470","39 - Chapter on what is said upon entering the mosque and leaving it. 375 - Ibn Abi Umar said: Al-Muqri narrated to us, Haywah ibn Shurayh narrated, Abu Sakhr informed me, from Yazid ibn Qusayt, from Abu al-Darda (may Allah be pleased with him), that he used to say: 'I surely say when I enter the mosque: Peace be upon you, O Messenger of Allah.' Halted; its men are the men of the Sahih, but it is disconnected."
"471","376 - [He said]: Waki' narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Sa'id ibn Abi Hind narrated, from more than one, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he went out to the mosque would say: 'O Allah, protect me from the accursed Satan.'"
"472","377 - Al-Harith said: Abd al-Aziz ibn [Aban] narrated to us, Hisham - that is al-Dastuwai - narrated, from Yahya - that is Ibn Abi Kathir - from Abdullah ibn Salam (may Allah be pleased with him): that when he entered the mosque he would greet the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then say: 'O Allah, open for me the doors of Your mercy'; and when he went out he would invoke blessings upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and seek refuge from Satan. Halted, and in it there is a break."
"473","378 - Abu Ya'la said: Suwayd ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Salih ibn Musa ibn Ishaq ibn Talhah narrated, from Abdullah ibn al-Hasan, from his mother Fatimah bint al-Husayn, from her father, from Ali (may Allah be pleased with them), who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he entered the mosque would say: 'O Allah, open for me the doors of Your mercy,' and when he went out he would say: 'O Allah, open for me the doors of Your bounty.' Layth ibn Abi Sulaym and others opposed him, saying: [from] Abdullah ibn al-Hasan, from his mother Fatimah, from her grandmother Fatimah, daughter of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"474","40 - Chapter on what is avoided in prayer and what is not avoided. 379/1 - Ishaq and Abu Bakr, both together, said: from Uqbah - Ishaq said: he informed us, and Abu Bakr said: Uqbah ibn Khalid al-Yashkuri narrated to us; Musa ibn Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Taymi narrated to me, from his father, that he narrated to him from Salamah ibn al-Akwa' (may Allah be pleased with him), that he asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about praying with the bow. He said: 'Pray with the bow, and cast aside the quiver.'"
"475","379/2 - Ishaq said: Isa ibn Yunus used to narrate it to us from Uqbah ibn Khalid, and Isa explained it, saying: The qaran is the small quiver carried by hunters."
"476","379/3 - Ishaq said: Abdullah ibn Nafi' al-Sa'igh informed us, from Musa, with this chain, the like of it."
"477","379/4 - Abu Ya'la said: Abu Bakr narrated to us, with it."
"478","380 - Ahmad ibn Mani' said: Yusuf narrated to us, from al-Ala, from Makhul, from Wathilah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: 'When we were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the military camp and prayer was established, we would leap to our bows and swords and pray in them as one does in a cloak.'"
"479","381 - [And] Musaddad said: Abd al-Warith narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Harith, from Ali (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: 'The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade me to pray while my hair was tied up, and to turn over pebbles in prayer...' the hadith."
"480","382 - Abd ibn Humayd said: Baqiyyah narrated to us, from Uthman ibn Zufar, from Hashim, from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: 'Whoever buys a garment for ten dirhams in which there is an unlawful dirham, Allah does not accept prayer from him so long as it is upon him.' Then he put his two fingers in his ears, then said: May they go deaf if the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not say it and we heard him say it."
"481","383 - [Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah] said: Abu Ghassan narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated, Abu Hamzah reported, from Ibrahim ibn Yazid, from Alqamah, from Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) removed his sandals while praying, so those behind him removed theirs. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'What made you remove your sandals?' They said: O Messenger of Allah, we saw you remove yours so we removed ours. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'Jibril (peace and blessings be upon him) informed me that there was filth on one of them, so I removed them for that; so do not remove your sandals.' Abu Hamzah is weak."
"482","384 - [Al-Harith] said: al-Hasan ibn Qutaybah narrated to us, Yazid ibn Ibrahim narrated, Bakr ibn Abdullah al-Muzani narrated, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed and removed his sandals, so the people removed their sandals. He said to them: 'Why did you remove your sandals?' They said: You removed yours so we removed ours. He said: 'Jibril (peace be upon him) informed me that there was harm in them; when one of you comes to the mosque let him turn over his sandals; if there is harm in them let him remove them, otherwise let him pray in them.' Disconnected (mursal)."
"483","385 - [He said]: Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Humayd narrated; one who heard al-A'rabi narrated to me, who said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying while wearing two sandals of camel hide. He said: Then he spat to his left, then rubbed where he spat with his sandal."
"484","386 - Abu Bakr said: Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated, from Abu Ishaq, from Alqamah ibn Qays - and he [Zuhayr] did not hear from Alqamah - who said: Abdullah visited Abu Musa in his house, and prayer time came. Abu Musa said: Step forward, O Abu Abd al-Rahman - for you are older than me and more knowledgeable. He said: No, rather you step forward, for we came to you in your house and your mosque, so you have more right. So Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him) stepped forward and removed his sandals. When he gave the salutation, Abdullah [said to] him: What did you intend by removing them?! Are you in the sacred valley of Tuwa?!"
"485","387 - Abu Ya'la said: Ibrahim - that is Ibn Ar'arah - narrated to us, Salm ibn Qutaybah narrated, from Umar ibn Nabhan, from Qatadah, from Anas (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: 'The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray in his leather socks.'"
"486","388 - Ishaq said: al-Mu'ammal reported to me, Sufyan narrated, from Mukhawwal ibn Rashid, from al-Maqburi, from Abu Rafi', from Umm Salamah, who said: 'The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade a man to pray with his head tied up in a knot.' I said to al-Mu'ammal: Is Umm Salamah in it? He said: I do not doubt; I wrote it from him first in Makkah. I said: Abd al-Razzaq and Waki' narrated it from Sufyan al-Thawri without Umm Salamah in it; Ahmad narrated it from both of them, and for that reason Ishaq questioned al-Mu'ammal. If al-Mu'ammal preserved it, the discrepancy is from Sufyan, not from him; and Allah knows best."
"487","41 - Chapter on the tooth-stick at every prayer. The hadith of Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr (may Allah be pleased with them both), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: 'Were it not that I would burden my community, I would command them to use the tooth-stick at every prayer,' already came in the chapter of the tooth-stick. 389 - Ishaq said: Jarir informed us, from Muslim al-A'war, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: 'Were it not that you would neglect it, I would command you to use the tooth-stick at every prayer.'"
"488","42 - Chapter on the rows. 390 - Musaddad said: Yahya narrated to us, from Ubayd Allah; Nafi' informed me, from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: 'When they are three, one of them steps forward and two step back, forming a row behind him.' He said: I came once and stood at his left, so he placed me at his right. Sahih, halted."
"489","391 - [Musaddad said]: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, from Abu Ma'mar, from Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: 'The women of the Children of Israel used to pray with the men in the row, so they took high wooden pattens to stretch themselves taller, so that one of them could look at her friend; so menstruation was imposed upon them and they were put behind. Abdullah said: So put them behind where Allah Almighty put them behind.'"
"490","392 - Yahya narrated to us, from Malik, from al-Zuhri, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah, from his father, who said: 'I entered with [Umar] at the forenoon prayer, and he placed me at his right; then Yarfa came, so I and he stood behind him.' Sahih, halted."
"491","393 - [Musaddad said]: Umar ibn Ali narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated, who said: I heard Abu [Sa'd] al-Khatmi say: I heard Jabir ibn Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrate: 'The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed with him and with Jabir - or Jabbar - ibn Sakhr, and placed them both behind him.' Its origin is in Muslim, in a long hadith through al-Walid ibn Ubadah, from Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him), with other than this wording."
"492","394/1 - Abu Bakr said: Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from al-Walid ibn Jumay', from one who narrated to him, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'Straighten the rows, for the devils slip among you as if they were the young of small sheep.'"
"493","394/2 - Abu Ya'la said: Abdullah ibn Umar ibn Aban narrated to us, Ibn Fudayl narrated, with it."
"494","395 - Al-Harith said: al-Khalil ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, Mujalid narrated, from al-Sha'bi, from Fatimah bint Qays (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: 'The best of the men's rows is the first of them, and the worst of them is the last of them; and the best of the women's rows is the last of them, and the worst of them is the first of them.'"
"495","396 - [Al-Harith said]: Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, Sufyan narrated, [or] al-Ashja'i, from Sufyan, from Ibrahim, from Umar (may Allah be pleased with him), that he said: 'Allah and His angels invoke blessings upon the one who maintains the first row.'"
"496","397 - [Musaddad] said: Yahya narrated to us, from Sufyan; Ammar al-Duhni narrated to me, from Hujayrah bint Husayn, who said: 'Umm Salamah (may Allah be pleased with her) led us in the afternoon prayer, standing among us.'"
"497","398 - Yahya narrated to us, from Sufyan; Ammar narrated to me, from Imran, from Suwayd ibn Ghaflah, who said: 'Bilal (may Allah be pleased with him) used to straighten our shoulders and strike our feet to straighten the row.' And the hadith of Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) will come in the chapter of saying Amin."
"498","43 - Chapter on congregational prayer. 399/1 - Ishaq said: Abu Amir Abd al-Malik ibn Amr al-Aqadi informed us, Ayyub ibn Sayyar al-Zuhri narrated, from Ya'qub ibn Zayd, from Abu Bahriyyah, who said: 'I entered the mosque of Hims, and there was a youth with people around him, curly-haired and very curly; when he spoke it was as if light and pearls came out of his mouth. I said: Who is this? They said: Mu'adh ibn Jabal (may Allah be pleased with him). Then I heard him say: Whoever is pleased to meet Allah Almighty safe, let him attend these five prayers where the call is made for them, for they are from the ways of guidance and from what your Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordained for you. Let him not say: I have a place of prayer in my house so I pray in it; for if you do that you abandon the way of your Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and if you abandon the way of your Prophet you will go astray. By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, I saw us in the time of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and none stayed back from it except a hypocrite of clear hypocrisy, until even the sick man would be supported between two men until he was placed in the row.'"
"499","399/2 - Abu Ya'la said: Abd al-A'la ibn Hammad narrated to us."
"500","400 - Abu Dawud said: Talhah ibn Amr narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him), raised: 'I intended to command a caller to call the prayer, then stay behind against men who stay back from prayer and burn their houses over them.'"
"501","401 - [Musaddad] said: Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated, from Thabit ibn Ubayd, who said: 'I visited Zayd ibn Thabit to see him while he was ill, and his two sons were with him; prayer was established, and he said: Go to prayer, for a man's prayer in congregation exceeds his prayer alone by twenty-five degrees.'"
"502","402 - Abu Ya'la said: Dawud ibn Rushayd narrated to us, Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated, from Abu Bakr al-Ansi; Zayd ibn Rufay' narrated to me, Maymun ibn Mihran narrated, from Abu Umamah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'A man's prayer alone in the path of Allah Almighty equals twenty-five prayers; his prayer among his company equals nine hundred prayers; and his prayer in congregation equals forty-nine thousand prayers.'"
"503","245 - [Al-Harith] said: Dawud narrated to us, Maysarah narrated, from Abu A'ishah, from Yazid ibn Umar, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah and Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them), who both said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed us and said: 'Whoever guards the congregation wherever he is and with whomever he is will cross the Bridge like flashing lightning in the first company with the foremost; his face will be brighter than the moon on the night of the full moon; and for every day and night he guards it he will have the reward of a martyr. Whoever guards the front row, catching the first takbir without harming a believer, Allah Almighty will give him the reward of the caller to prayer on the Day of Resurrection.' Then he mentioned the hadith on the reward of the callers to prayer, which already came in the chapter of the call to prayer. This is a fabricated hadith which al-Harith cited in about five pages."
"504","403 - Musaddad said: Yahya narrated to us, from Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah, from Abu Musa al-Hilali, from his father, from Ibn Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: 'Whoever hears the call to prayer then does not come to prayer without an excuse, there is no prayer for him.'"
"505","404 - Hushaym narrated to us, from Mughirah, from Ibrahim: 'That he disliked a man leaving the mosque after he heard the call to commence prayer.'"
"506","405 - Ibn Abi Shaybah said: Ghundar narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman - that is Ibn Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn As'ad ibn Zurarah - from his uncle - that is Yahya ibn As'ad ibn Zurarah, who said: I never saw among us a man resembling him - narrating from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: 'Whoever hears the congregational call then does not come, three times, then hears then does not come, three times, his heart is sealed and his heart is made the heart of a hypocrite.'"
"507","406 - [Al-Harith] said: Dawud ibn al-Muhabbar narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sa'id narrated, from Aban ibn Abi Ayyash, from Anas ibn Malik (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'The merit of a man's prayer in congregation over his prayer alone is twenty-four parts.' And the hadith of Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from a man of the Companions (may Allah be pleased with them), will come in the chapter of heart-softeners, Allah willing."
"508","407 - Abu Ya'la said: Muhammad ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Zibriqan Abu Hammam narrated, Musa ibn Ubaydah narrated; Abu Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hazm informed me, from Abbad ibn Tamim, from Abdullah ibn Zayd (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: 'Allah Almighty and His angels invoke blessings upon those who join the rows; and between the prayer of the lone man and the congregation there are twenty-five degrees.'"
"509","44 - Chapter on the minimum congregation. 408 - Abu Ya'la said: Muhammad ibn Bakkar narrated to us, Ibn al-Mubarak narrated, from Yahya ibn Ayyub, from Ubayd Allah ibn Zahr, from Ali ibn Yazid, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: A man came as a delegation, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'Is there no man to give charity to this one and pray with him?' So a man stood and prayed with him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'This is the congregation, and these are a congregation.'"
"510","45 - Chapter on guarding the congregation. 409 - Musaddad said: Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, al-Awza'i narrated, from Umayr ibn Hani, who said: 'I witnessed Abdullah ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) in Makkah, while al-Hajjaj was besieging Ibn al-Zubayr (may Allah be pleased with them both); Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) was between the two, and he would sometimes attend prayer with these and sometimes attend prayer with those.' Its chain is sahih."
"511","410 - Abu Dawud said: Muhammad ibn [Abi] Humayd narrated to us, from Abu Abdullah al-Qarraz, from Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'The hypocrite does not guard the last night prayer for forty nights' - meaning in congregation."
"512","46 - Chapter on the command to follow the imam in his actions. 411 - Abu Bakr said: Khalid ibn Makhlad narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated, from Ja'far ibn Muhammad, who said: I heard al-Qasim ibn Muhammad say: Mu'awiyah ibn Abi Sufyan (may Allah be pleased with them both) said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'When the imam prays sitting, pray sitting.' He said: So the people marvelled at the truthfulness of Mu'awiyah (may Allah be pleased with him)."
"513","412 - Abu Ya'la said: al-Hasan ibn Isma'il al-Basri Abu Sa'id narrated to us, Ibrahim - meaning Ibn Sa'd - narrated, from his father, from his grandfather, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: 'When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) reached Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf (may Allah be pleased with him) while he was leading the people in prayer, Abd al-Rahman wanted to step back, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) signalled to him: Stay in your place. So he prayed, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed following the prayer of Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf (may Allah be pleased with him).'"
"514","413 - Abd ibn Humayd said: Abdullah ibn Maslamah narrated to us, Khalid ibn Ilyas narrated, from Ibrahim ibn Ubayd ibn Rifa'ah, who said: I visited Jabir ibn Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with them both) and found him sitting, leading his companions in the afternoon prayer while they sat. He said: I watched until he gave the salutation, then said: May Allah forgive you - you, a Companion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), leading them while sitting? He said: I am ill, so I sat, and I commanded them to sit. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: 'The imam is a shield; when he prays standing, pray standing, and when he prays sitting, pray sitting.'"
"515","414 - Abu Bakr said: al-Fadl ibn Dukayn narrated to us, Umar ibn Musa narrated; Musa ibn Abdullah ibn Yazid reported, from his father (may Allah be pleased with him), that he used to lead the people in prayer here; some people would place their heads before he placed his head and raise their heads before he raised his head. When he finished he turned to them and said: O people, why do you sin and cause sin? I prayed for you the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) without falling short of it."
"516","415 - Musaddad said: Muhammad ibn Jabir narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Badr narrated, from Ali ibn Shayban, from his father (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: I prayed behind the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and a man raised his head before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). When he finished he said: 'Whoever raises his head before the imam, or lowers it, there is no prayer for him.'"
"517","416/1 - Al-Humaydi said: Sufyan narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Amr narrated; I heard Mulayh ibn Abdullah narrate from Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: 'Whoever raises his head and lowers it before the imam, his forelock is in the hand of a devil.' He said: Sufyan would sometimes raise it (to the Prophet) and sometimes not raise it. 416/2 - Al-Bazzar narrated it through Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad, from Muhammad ibn Amr, and said: We do not know of Mulayh narrating from Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) except this."
"518","417 - [Musaddad] said: Mu'tamir narrated to us, who said: I heard my father narrate from a man, from Anas (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: 'When we raised our heads from bowing behind the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), we would remain standing until we saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prostrate and place his face firmly on the ground, then we would prostrate after that.' And the hadith of Abd al-Aziz ibn Rufay', from an elder of the Ansar (may Allah be pleased with him), will come in the description of prayer, Allah willing."
"519","47 - Chapter on the sin of one who is not moderate in his leading. 245 - Al-Harith said: Dawud ibn al-Muhabbar narrated to us, Maysarah ibn Abd Rabbihi narrated, from Abu A'ishah al-Sa'di, from Yazid ibn Umar, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurayrah and Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), who both said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed us, then mentioned a long hadith in which: 'Whoever leads a people while they are pleased with him, and is moderate with them in his presence of heart, recitation, bowing, prostration and sitting, he has the like of their rewards; and whoever is not moderate with them in that, his prayer is thrown back at him and does not pass beyond his collarbones, and he is like an unjust, transgressing ruler who did not act rightly toward his subjects nor uphold among them the command of Allah Almighty.' Ali ibn Abi Talib (may Allah be pleased with him) said: O Messenger of Allah, may my father and mother be sacrificed for you, what is the station of the unjust, transgressing ruler who did not act rightly toward his subjects nor uphold among them the command of Allah Almighty? He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'He is the fourth of four, and he is the most severely punished of people on the Day of Resurrection: Iblis, Pharaoh, Qabil the killer of the soul, and the unjust ruler is their fourth.' This is a fabricated hadith."
"520","48 - Chapter on commanding the imam to lighten. 418 - [Ishaq] said: Yahya ibn Hammad al-Basri informed us, Abu Awanah narrated, al-A'mash narrated, Abu Salih narrated, from Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'Be brief in prayer, for behind you are the weak, the elderly, and the one with a need.'"
"521","419/1 - Al-A'mash said: Ibrahim narrated to us, from al-Harith ibn Suwayd, from Abdullah, the like of that."
"522","419/2 - He said: Ibrahim al-Nakha'i narrated to us from Abdullah the like of that."
"523","420 - He said: Habib ibn Abi Thabit narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with the like of that. I said: The hadith of Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) has been narrated by them."
"524","421 - [And] Abu Ya'la said: Ahmad ibn Isa al-Misri narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated; Sa'id ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Amya narrated to me, who said: Sahl ibn Abi Umamah ibn Sahl narrated to him: that he and his father visited Anas ibn Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) in the time of Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz (may Allah be pleased with him), while he was a governor; he prayed a light prayer as if it were a traveller's prayer or close to it. When he gave the salutation he said: May Allah have mercy on you, [have you seen] this prayer - is it the obligatory one or something voluntary you prayed? He said: It is the obligatory one, and it is the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); I did not miss anything of it [except something] I forgot. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: 'Do not be hard upon yourselves lest it be made hard upon you; for a people were hard upon themselves so it was made hard upon them - those are their remnants in the monasteries and cloisters: And monasticism which they invented, We did not prescribe it for them.'"
"525","422 - Ahmad ibn Mani' said: Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, al-Hajjaj and Ibn Abi Layla narrated, from al-Asbagh ibn Nubatah, from Ali (may Allah be pleased with him), that he narrated to them that Mu'adh (may Allah be pleased with him) led his people in the dawn prayer and recited Surah al-Baqarah, while behind him was a Bedouin man with a water-carrying camel of his. In the second rak'ah the Bedouin prayed (alone) and left Mu'adh (may Allah be pleased with him). They reported it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: I feared for my water-camel, and I have dependents [I earn for] upon it. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'Lead them in the prayer of the weakest of them, for among them are the young, the elderly and the one with a need; [do not be a source of trial].'"
"526","49 - Chapter on prompting the imam. 423 - Ahmad ibn Mani' said: Muhammad ibn Mubashshir Abu Sa'd al-Saghani narrated to us, Isra'il narrated, from Abd al-A'la, from Abu Abd al-Rahman, who said: Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) said: 'It is from the Sunnah to prompt the imam when he asks you for it.' I said to Abu Abd al-Rahman: What is the imam asking for? He said: When he falls silent."
"527","424 - Al-Harith said: Asim ibn Ali narrated to us, Qays ibn al-Rabi' narrated, from al-Agharr, from Khalifah ibn Husayn, from Abu Nasr - that is al-Asadi - from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: 'The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) hesitated over a verse in the dawn prayer; when he finished the prayer he looked at the faces of the people and said: 'Was Ubayy ibn Ka'b not praying with you?' They said: No. He said: Then the people thought he had missed him only so that he would prompt him.'"
"528","50 - Chapter on repeating prayer in congregation in the mosque. 425 - Abu Ya'la said: Abu al-Rabi' al-Zahrani narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated, from al-Ja'd Abu Uthman, who said: 'Anas ibn Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) passed by us in the mosque of Banu Tha'labah and said: Have you prayed? We said: Yes - that was at the dawn prayer - so he commanded a man, who called the adhan and the iqamah, then he led his companions in prayer.' Sahih, halted."
"529","51 - Chapter on the prohibition of pushing one another forward for leadership after the imam. 226 - Ishaq said: Abd al-Razzaq reported to me; I heard my father narrate from one of the scholars, who said: 'Prayer was established, and the people pushed the leadership onto one another; each kept saying to the other: Step forward, until the earth swallowed them.'"
"530","52 - Chapter on the measure of recitation in prayer. 427 - [Ishaq] said: Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ma'mar narrated; a man narrated, from al-Hasan, from Ubadah ibn al-Samit (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: 'The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited at the night prayer on a journey with By the Fig and the Olive.' This is disconnected in [two places], and it has a witness in the Sahih from the hadith of al-Bara ibn Azib (may Allah be pleased with them both)."
"531","428 - [Ishaq said]: Yahya ibn Adam informed us, Mindal al-Anazi narrated, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated, from Ali ibn Yahya ibn Khallad, from his uncle (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: 'The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite in the first two rak'ahs the Opening of the Book and a surah, and in the last two the Opening of the Book.' This is a weak chain."
"532","429 - Musaddad said: Yahya narrated to us, from Thawr; Khalid ibn Ma'dan narrated to me, from Abdullah ibn Ubayd al-Thumali - who was among the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - and from al-Hajjaj ibn Amir al-Thumali - who was among the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - (may Allah be pleased with them both): 'That they both prayed with Umar ibn al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) [the dawn prayer], and he recited: When the sky is rent asunder, and prostrated in it.'"
"533","430 - Yazid narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated, from Sa'd ibn Ibrahim, from Abdullah ibn Tha'labah, who said: 'I prayed with Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) the dawn prayer, and he recited al-Hajj in it, prostrating twice in it.' I said: The dawn? He said: 'The dawn.'"
"534","431 - Al-Harith said: Muhammad ibn Umar narrated to us, [Ali ibn Abdullah, from Abu Yahya al-Aslami] narrated, from Bukayr ibn al-Ashajj, from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Ayyub (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited at dawn: Blessed is He in Whose Hand is the dominion."
"535","432 - Al-Harith said: Muhammad ibn Umar narrated to us, Dawud ibn Khalid ibn Dinar narrated, from Yazid ibn Abdullah ibn Qusayt, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: 'The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded me to recite at dawn with By the night when it covers, and By the sun and its brightness.' [I said: Muhammad ibn Umar in this and the one before it is al-Waqidi, and he is abandoned.]"
"536","433 - Abu Ya'la said: Khalifah ibn Khayyat narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Uthman narrated, Mughallis al-Khurasani narrated, from Ayyub ibn Yazid, from Abu Razin, from Amr ibn Abasah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited at dawn: Say: I seek refuge with the Lord of the daybreak, and Say: I seek refuge with the Lord of mankind. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'Al-Falaq is Hell.'"
"537","53 - Chapter on holding Friday congregation in houses. 413 - Abd [ibn Humayd] said: Abdullah ibn Maslamah narrated to us, Khalid ibn Ilyas narrated, from Ibrahim ibn Ubayd ibn Rifa'ah, who said: I visited Jabir ibn Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with them both) in Makkah and found him sitting, leading his companions in prayer ... the hadith, and in it: 'We would call out in our houses for prayer, and hold the Friday gathering for our families.'"
"538","54 - Chapter on the conditions of imams. 434 - Al-Harith said: Dawud ibn al-Muhabbar narrated to us, [Anbasah] ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated, from Allaq Abu Muslim, from Anas ibn Malik (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'The imam of a people is their delegate to Allah Almighty, so put forward the best of you.'"
"539","435 - [He said]: Abd al-Aziz ibn Aban narrated to us, Sufyan narrated, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Abu Salih, who said: 'Mu'adh (may Allah be pleased with him) used to pray the dawn prayer with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then return and lead his companions.' Disconnected (mursal)."
"540","436 - [Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah] said: Abu Usamah narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid ibn Jabir, who said: I heard al-Qasim ibn Mukhaymirah say: Salman's people put him forward to lead them in prayer, and he refused until they pushed him. When he led them he said: 'Are all of you pleased?' They said: Yes. He said: Praise be to Allah; I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: 'There are three whose prayer is not accepted: the woman who leaves her house without her husband's permission, the runaway slave, and the man who leads a people while they dislike him.'"
"541","437 - [Musaddad] said: Hafs narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj, who said: 'Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) used to dislike one performing dry ablution leading those performing ablution.'"
"542","438 - Yahya narrated to us, from Shu'bah, from Sa'd ibn Ibrahim, from his father, who said: 'Mu'awiyah (may Allah be pleased with him) led them wearing a shirt.'"
"543","439 - [Al-Harith] said: Dawud ibn Rushayd narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Maryam narrated, from Abu al-Ahwas and Damrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'O Abu Ubaydah, let no one after me lead sitting.'"
"544","55 - Chapter on what one who comes alone and finds the row complete should do. 440 - Abu Ya'la said: Abu Ubaydah ibn al-Fudayl ibn Iyad narrated to us, Malik ibn Sa'd narrated, al-Sari ibn Isma'il narrated, from al-Sha'bi, from Wabisah ibn Ma'bad, who said: 'The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished prayer while a man was praying behind the people alone, so he said: O you who prays alone, did you not join a row and enter with them, or draw a man to you if the place was tight for you? Repeat your prayer, for there is no prayer for you.'"
"545","56 - Chapter on making up missed prayers. 441 - Abu Ya'la said: Zuhayr narrated to us, Mu'adh ibn Hisham narrated; my father narrated to me, from Amir, from Abu Sa'id (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - concerning one who forgets a prayer - who said: 'He prays it when he remembers it.'"
"546","442/1 - Abu Bakr said: al-Fadl ibn Dukayn narrated to us, from Abd al-Jabbar ibn Ayyash, from Awn ibn Abi Juhayfah, from his father (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - on his journey in which they slept - when the sun rose upon them, said (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): 'You were dead, then Allah Almighty returned your souls to you; whoever sleeps past a prayer, let him pray it when he wakes, and whoever forgets a prayer, let him pray it when he remembers it.'"
"547","442/2 - Abu Ya'la said: Zuhayr narrated to us, al-Fadl ibn Dukayn narrated, with it."
"548","443 - Musaddad said: al-Mu'tamir narrated to us; I heard Layth narrate from Nu'aym ibn Abi Hind, from Rib'i ibn [Hirash], from Silah, who said: 'Hudhayfah (may Allah be pleased with him) appointed me as his deputy; we prayed the noon prayer, then came upon people praying noon and prayed with them; then we prayed the afternoon prayer, then came upon people praying afternoon and prayed with them; then we prayed the sunset prayer, then came upon people praying sunset and prayed with them; when I stood for the third (rak'ah) he held me back.'"
"549","444 - Yahya narrated to us, from Mis'ar, from Abd al-Malik ibn Maysarah, from al-Nazzal ibn Sabrah, who said: 'Al-Walid ibn Uqbah (may Allah be pleased with him) led the people in prayer, then Abdullah repeated the prayer with the people and repeated the prayer.'"
"550","445 - Abu Ya'la said: Abu Ibrahim al-Tarjuman narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Jumahi narrated, from Ubayd Allah, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'Whoever forgets a prayer and remembers it only while he is with the imam, let him pray with the imam; when he finishes his prayer let him repeat the prayer he forgot, then let him repeat the prayer he prayed with the imam.'"
"551","446 - Abu Bakr said: Abidah ibn Humayd narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Tamim ibn Salamah, from Masruq, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: 'The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out and camped at night; he did not wake except by the sun. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded Bilal (may Allah be pleased with him), who called the adhan, then he prayed two rak'ahs.' Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) said: Nothing of the world and what is in it would delight me as it does - meaning the concession."
"552","5 - Description of Prayer. 1 - Chapter on the opening and other matters. The hadith of opening prayer with the takbir will come, Allah willing, in the chapter of the salutation. 447/1 - Ishaq: al-Nadr ibn Shumayl informed us, Shu'bah narrated, from Husayn, from Abdullah ibn Shaddad, that he heard Rifa'ah ibn Rafi' - a man of the people of Badr -: 'He said the takbir in his prayer, saying: Allah is Greatest; O Allah, all praise is Yours, all dominion is Yours, and to You returns the whole affair; I ask You for all good, and I seek refuge in You from all evil.' I said: Al-Bukhari narrated in his Sahih from Adam, from Shu'bah, from Husayn, from Ibn Shaddad, who said: 'I saw Rifa'ah ibn Rafi' al-Ansari, who had witnessed Badr' - and the rest is upon his condition, though here it is not raised; and I think its ruling is that of a raised narration."
"553","447/2 - Ishaq: Abu Amir al-Aqadi informed us, Shu'bah narrated, from Husayn, [who said]: I heard Abdullah ibn Shaddad ibn al-Had, that he heard a man of the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called Rifa'ah ibn Rafi' say: When he entered prayer he said the takbir, then said: then he mentioned the like of it. This is a sahih hadith."
"554","448 - Musaddad said: Attaf ibn Khalid narrated to us; Isma'il ibn Rafi' narrated to me, from Anas ibn Malik (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: I was sitting with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the mosque of al-Khayf, when two men came to him: an Ansari and a Thaqafi. Then he mentioned the hadith. He said: The Thaqafi said: Inform me, O Messenger of Allah, about what I came to ask you. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'You came to ask me about prayer.' Then he mentioned the hadith. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'Then when you stand for prayer, recite what is easy of the Qur'an; then when you bow, place your hands firmly upon your knees and spread your fingers until you are settled bowing; then when you prostrate, place your face firmly in prostration until you are settled prostrating; and pray at the beginning of the night and its end.' He said: What if I pray the whole night? He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'Then you are as you are.'"
"555","449 - Ibn Abi Shaybah said: Shabbabah narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Dhi'b, who said: Sa'id ibn Sam'an narrated to me, who said: Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) came to us and said: 'The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pause before recitation for a short while, asking Allah from His bounty.'"
"556","450 - Al-Harith said: Muhammad ibn Umar narrated to us, Ya'qub ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Sa'sa'ah narrated, from Ayyub ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Sa'sa'ah, from Abbad ibn Tamim, from Abdullah ibn Zayd (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: 'The opening of prayer is purification, its prohibition is the takbir, and its release is the salutation.'"
"557","2 - Chapter on when to stand for prayer. 451 - Abu Ya'la said: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Sahm al-Antaki narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn Farrukh narrated, al-Awwam ibn Hawshab narrated, from Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: 'When Bilal (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Prayer has been established, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would rise.'"
"558","452 - Abdan narrated to us, Abd al-Wahid narrated, Yunus ibn Ubayd narrated, who said: 'Al-Hasan (may Allah be pleased with him) used to dislike saying the takbir until the caller finished the iqamah.'"
"559","3 - Chapter on when to say the first takbir. 453 - Musaddad said: Yahya narrated to us, from Ibn Ajlan; al-A'raj narrated to me, from Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), concerning a man who enters the mosque while the people are bowing - should he say the takbir? He said: No, until you take your place in the row. Sahih, halted."
"560","454 - Ibn Abi Umar said: Yusuf ibn Khalid al-Basri narrated to us, from Juwaybir, from al-Dahhak, from Hudhayfah (may Allah be pleased with him): that he entered while the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was bowing, so he bowed short of the row; they mentioned his deed to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Hudhayfah did well and beautifully. This is a very feeble chain."
"561","456 - Abu Bakr said: Abu Usamah narrated to us, from Abu Farwah: Yazid ibn Sinan; Abu Ubayd al-Hajib narrated, who said: I heard an elder in the Sacred Mosque say: Abu al-Darda (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'Everything has a prime part, and the prime part of prayer is the first takbir; so guard it.' Abu Ubayd said: I narrated it to Raja ibn Haywah, who said: Umm al-Darda narrated to me, from Abu al-Darda (may Allah be pleased with them both). Its chain is good."
"562","457 - Musaddad said: Yahya narrated to us, from Awf, from al-Hasan, who said: 'It reached me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say when opening prayer: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the accursed Satan, from his madness, his poetry and his arrogance.' It was said: What is his madness? He said: His madness is the seizure that takes the children of Adam; his poetry-breath is poetry; and his arrogant breath is pride."
"563","458 - Abu Ya'la said: Ishaq ibn Abi Isra'il narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Jabir narrated, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: I prayed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and Abu Bakr and Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both), and they did not raise their hands except at the opening of prayer. And he said: They did not raise their hands after the first takbir. The authors of the Sunan narrated it with the wording: He did not raise his hands except at the first takbir."
"564","459 - Ahmad ibn Mani' said: I witnessed Salamah ibn Salih narrate from Ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raise his hands when opening prayer, when bowing, and when raising his head from bowing."
"565","460 - Musaddad said: Yahya narrated to us, Thawr ibn Yazid narrated, from Khalid ibn Ma'dan, from Abu Ziyad, freedman of the family of Darij, who said: Whatever I saw and forgot, I have not forgotten that Abu Bakr al-Siddiq (may Allah be pleased with him), when he stood in prayer, stood thus, taking with his right palm upon his left forearm, clinging at the elbow."
"566","461/1 - Ahmad ibn Mani' said: Abd al-Quddus ibn Bakr ibn Khunays narrated to us; al-Hajjaj reported, from Amir ibn Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr, from his father (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) open prayer, raising his hands until they passed beyond his ears."
"567","461/2 - Abu Ya'la said: Ahmad ibn Mani' narrated to us with this."
"568","462 - Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah said: Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Mu'awiyah ibn Salih narrated, Yunus ibn Sayf al-Ansi narrated, from al-Harith ibn Ghudayf - or Ghudayf ibn al-Harith al-Kindi, Mu'awiyah doubted - who said: Whatever I forget, I have not forgotten that I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) placing his right hand upon his left hand - meaning in prayer."
"569","463 - Ibn Abi Umar said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us; Ma'mar reported, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from a man, from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: A man came while the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was in prayer, and said - when he reached the row -: Allah is Greatest, greatly; praise be to Allah, abundantly; glory be to Allah, morning and evening. When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished his prayer he said: Who is the author of the words? The man said: I am, O Messenger of Allah, and I intended by them only good. He said: I saw the gates of heaven opened for them. Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: I have not left them since I heard them."
"570","464 - Abu Bakr said: Shadhan - al-Aswad ibn Amir - narrated to us, Sharik narrated, from Asim ibn Ubayd Allah, from Abdullah ibn Amir ibn Rabi'ah, from his father, who said: 'A man stood behind the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - while he was in prayer - and said: Praise be to Allah, abundant, good, blessed. When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished his prayer he said: Who is the speaker? A man of the people said: I am. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I saw twelve angels racing to it, which of them would write it.'"
"571","4 - Chapter on recitation in prayer and the reason for lightening it. 465 - Abu Ya'la said: al-Azraq ibn Ali narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr narrated, Abbad ibn Kathir narrated, from Thabit, from Anas (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) missed a man ... then he mentioned the hadith. He said: The man said: I passed by you, O Messenger of Allah, while you were praying Maghrib; I prayed with you, and you were reciting this surah: al-Qari'ah."
"572","466 - Abu Bakr said: Husayn ibn Ali narrated to us, from Za'idah, from Ibn Khuthaym; Dawud ibn Asim al-Thaqafi narrated to me, from Uthman ibn Abi al-As (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) set for me to recite with: Glorify the Name of your Lord, the Most High, and its like from the Qur'an."
"573","467 - Abd al-Salam ibn Harb narrated to me, from Layth, from Shahr, from Abu Malik (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite in the four (rak'ahs) of noon and afternoon."
"574","468 - Musaddad said: Yahya narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik, from Ata, from Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: Whoever recites the Opening of the Book in the obligatory prayer, it suffices him; and if he adds something with it, it is dearer to me."
"575","469 - Abd al-Warith narrated to us, Hanzalah al-Sadusi narrated, who said: I said to Ikrimah: I sometimes recite at Maghrib: Say: I seek refuge with the Lord of the daybreak, and Say: I seek refuge with the Lord of mankind, yet people blame me for it!? He said: Glory be to Allah! Recite them both, for they are from the Qur'an."
"576","470 - Abu Dawud said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Hayyan al-Bariqi; it was said to Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) - or a man said to him -: I pray behind so-and-so, and he lengthens the prayer. He said: Two rak'ahs of the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) were lighter than a rak'ah of so-and-so's prayer, or were like so-and-so's prayer, or like a rak'ah of so-and-so's prayer."
"577","471/1 - Ibn Abi Shaybah said: Sharik ibn Abdullah narrated to us, from Abu Harun - as far as he knows - from Abu Sa'id (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led them in the dawn prayer and recited for them the two shortest surahs of the Qur'an, or the briefest. He said: When he finished prayer, Abu Sa'id al-Khudri - or Mu'adh (may Allah be pleased with them both) - said to him: O Messenger of Allah, I saw you pray a prayer the like of which I never saw you pray. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'Did you not hear the crying of the infant behind me in the women's row? I wanted to free his mother for him.'"
"578","471/2 - Abd ibn Humayd said: Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, Sufyan narrated, from Abu Harun, who said: I heard Abu Sa'id al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) say: He led us in prayer, then he mentioned it."
"579","472 - Abu Ya'la said: Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj narrated to us, Sukayn - that is Ibn Abd al-Aziz - narrated, al-Muthanna al-Attar narrated; Abd al-Aziz - meaning the father of al-Sukayn - narrated, who said: I came to Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) and said: Inform me about the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So he led his household, praying with us noon and afternoon, reciting softly; he recited al-Mursalat, al-Nazi'at, Amma yatasa'alun, and their like from the surahs."
"580","473 - Ibn Abi Umar said: al-Muqri narrated to us, Haywah narrated, Ja'far ibn Rabi'ah narrated, from al-A'raj, who said: Mu'awiyah ibn Abdullah narrated from Ibn Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him): that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited at Maghrib: Ha-Mim - the one in which the Smoke is mentioned."
"581","Abu Bakr said: Waki narrated to us, from Israil, from Jabir, from Amir, from Abdullah ibn Yazid (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited in Maghrib: By the fig and the olive."
"582","Abd ibn Humayd said: Abu Nuaym narrated to us, Israil narrated to us with the same chain."
"583","Chapter of saying Amin. Musaddad said: Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Mansur ibn al-Mutamir, from Mujahid, he said: A Jew passed by the people of a mosque while they were saying: Amin. The Jew said: By the One Who taught you Amin, you are indeed upon the truth."
"584","Al-Harith said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Aban narrated to us, Zarbi the freed slave of Khallad narrated to us, Anas ibn Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated to us, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have been given three qualities: prayer in rows, and I have been given peace, which is the greeting of the people of Paradise, and I have been given Amin, and none of those before you was given it, except that Allah, Blessed and Exalted, gave it to Harun, for Musa (peace be upon him) used to supplicate and Harun (peace be upon him) used to say Amin. I say: Ibn Khuzaymah brought it in his Sahih by another route from Zarbi, but he said: Ibn Bint al-Hurr. I say: It is not established due to the weakness of Zarbi."
"585","Ishaq said: al-Nadr ibn Shumayl narrated to us, from Harun al-Awar, from Ismail ibn Muslim, from Abu Ishaq, from Ibn Umm al-Husayn, from his mother, that she prayed behind the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and she heard him saying: Master of the Day of Judgment, and when he recited: nor of those who go astray, he said: Amin, until she heard him while she was in the row of women."
"586","Chapter of the obligation of recitation in prayer upon the imam and the follower, and of one who dropped recitation for the one who catches the first rakah in particular. Musaddad said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: Whoever catches the people bowing, that rakah shall not be counted."
"587","Yahya narrated to us, from Sufyan, Abd al-Aziz ibn Rufay narrated to me, from a shaykh of the Ansar, he said: A man entered the mosque, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard the shuffling of his sandals, and when he gave salam he said: How did you catch us? He said: In prostration, so I prostrated. He said: Do likewise, and do not count the prostration as long as you do not catch the rakah; when you see the imam standing, then stand, and bowing, then bow, and prostrating, then prostrate, and sitting, then sit. Sahih."
"588","Chapter of Qunut. Al-Harith said: Yahya ibn Hashim narrated to us, Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, from his father, from Aishah (may Allah be pleased with her), she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to make qunut in Fajr before the bowing, and he said: I only make qunut with you so that you supplicate to your Lord and ask Him your needs. Yahya is very weak."
"589","Ibn Abi Umar said: Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Aban, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: He spent the night with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he made qunut before the bowing, then I sent my mother the next year, and she informed me of the same."
"590","Ahmad ibn Mani said: Yazid narrated to us, Aban ibn Abi Ayyash narrated to us, and he mentioned it with the wording: I spent the night with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to see how he makes qunut in his witr, and he made qunut before bowing, then I sent my mother Umm Abd and said: Spend the night with his wives (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and see how he makes qunut in his witr, and she informed me that he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made qunut before bowing. Aban is abandoned."
"591","Ahmad ibn Mani said: Yaqub Abu Yusuf narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Abu al-Hasan, from Said ibn Zayd, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made qunut and said: O Allah, suffice me against Ril, Dhakwan, Adal and Usayyah who disobeyed Allah and His Messenger."
"592","Ibn Abi Shaybah said: Malik ibn Ismail narrated to us, from Sharik, from Abu Hamzah, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not make qunut except for a month; he did not make qunut before it nor after it. Abu Hamzah is Maymun al-Awar, weak."
"593","Abu Yala said: Bishr, that is Ibn al-Walid, narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, and he mentioned it with the wording: He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made qunut for a month supplicating against Usayyah and Dhakwan, and when he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prevailed over them, he left qunut."
"594","Al-Harith said: al-Sakan ibn Nafi narrated to us, Imran ibn Hudayr narrated to us, he said: Qunut in the morning prayer was mentioned to Abu Mijlaz, and he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent a man to Banu so-and-so and said: Look, if they have called the adhan, pass them by to Banu so-and-so; when he came to them asking them, a man entered, put on his armor, meaning his weapon, then went out to the messenger of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stabbing him, and threw him down. The messenger of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, I am the messenger of Your Messenger, convey to him salam from me. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: And upon you be peace. The people said: O Messenger of Allah, we did not see anyone. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: So-and-so was killed, and he sent me salam. He stood with them for a month at the end of Fajr prayer saying: O Allah, upon Banu Usayyah, they disobeyed their Lord, and upon Banu Dhakwan. Then he left it; there was nothing else. Mursal."
"595","Ahmad ibn Mani said: Yazid narrated to us, Sulayman al-Taymi informed us, from Abu Mijlaz, he said: I said to Ibn Umar and Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them): Does old age prevent you from qunut? They said: We did not take it from our companions. Sahih mawquf."
"596","Chapter of placing the right hand upon the left. Al-Tayalisi said: Talhah, that is Ibn Amr, narrated to us, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: We, the company of the prophets, were commanded to hasten our breaking of the fast, and to delay our suhur, and to place our right hands upon our left hands in prayer."
"597","Abd ibn Humayd said: Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Talhah ibn Amr narrated to us, and he mentioned it with the wording: We, the company of the prophets, were commanded to delay our suhur, and to hold with our hands upon our left hands in prayer."
"598","Ahmad ibn Mani said: Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, Talhah narrated to us with it. Gharib, Talhah ibn Amr al-Makki alone narrated it, and there is weakness in him. Ahmad ibn Tahir ibn Harmalah al-Tujibi brought in it a rejected oddity, he said: My grandfather narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, from Amr ibn al-Harith, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), mentioning it, but he erred in his saying: from Amr ibn al-Harith, for it is only Talhah ibn Amr; and Ahmad ibn Tahir was declared a liar by al-Daraqutni and others, and al-Tabarani brought it in al-Awsat from Ahmad ibn Tahir."
"599","Chapter of humility. Al-Harith said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Aban narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Harith, he said: A man narrated to him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah the Exalted continues to turn to the servant in his prayer as long as he does not turn away. That man who narrated this hadith to me, when he stood in prayer, was as if he were a peg."
"600","Abu Yala said: al-Abbas ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Yusuf ibn Khalid narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Anas (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a man moving pebbles while in prayer, and when he finished he said to the man: That is your share of your prayer."
